OFFLINE_LIBRARY.push(...[{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-8310","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Friends","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"9 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Friends</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-60452","sourceQuestionId":60452,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you have a friend you have known for a long time?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60453","sourceQuestionId":60453,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you often go out with your friends?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60454","sourceQuestionId":60454,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you prefer to spend time with one friend or with a group of friends?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60455","sourceQuestionId":60455,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"How important are friends to you?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60456","sourceQuestionId":60456,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Is there a difference between where you meet friends now and where you used to meet them in the past?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60457","sourceQuestionId":60457,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"What do you usually do with your friends?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60458","sourceQuestionId":60458,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Where do you often meet each other?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60459","sourceQuestionId":60459,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Why are some places suitable for meeting while others are not?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60460","sourceQuestionId":60460,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Would you invite friends to your home?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["准备一位亲近朋友和一次共同活动。用具体相处方式解释友谊，而不是只列 friendly、kind。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60452","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Yes, my closest friend is someone I met on my first day of primary school.","We’ve maintained our friendship for over two decades, navigating different schools, universities, and cities."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60453","approach":"先给频率，再补一项真实活动或原因。","example_direction":["I would say we have a good balance.","We make a point to schedule proper outings, like trying a new restaurant or going to an exhibition, a couple of times a month."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60454","approach":"先表达偏好，再解释选择标准；可以补一句例外。","example_direction":["I appreciate both dynamics for different reasons.","One-on-one time allows for deeper, more intimate and vulnerable conversations."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60455","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["They are utterly vital.","My friends are my chosen family; they provide a crucial support system, emotional sustenance, and shared joy."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60456","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["There's a significant difference.","In our teens and early twenties, we almost exclusively met in public places like shopping malls, cinemas, or fast-food restaurants."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60457","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Our activities are quite varied.","We often go out for meals or coffee to catch up, go for walks in the park, or watch films together."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60458","approach":"先给具体地点，再说明选择这个地点的原因或一个相关场景。","example_direction":["We tend to favour casual, comfortable environments where we can talk without shouting.","Our most common meeting spots are cosy cafés, each other's homes, or parks when the weather is nice."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60459","approach":"先给直接理由，再用一个日常细节说明；无需长篇背景。","example_direction":["Suitability hinges on the desired interaction.","A noisy sports bar is perfect for watching a match with a group but terrible for a heart-to-heart conversation."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60460","approach":"给一个具体设想，说明条件与原因，避免把未发生的事说成已发生。","example_direction":["Absolutely.","I consider it the highest form of hospitality and intimacy."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60452","text":"Yes, my closest friend is someone I met on my first day of primary school. We’ve maintained our friendship for over two decades, navigating different schools, universities, and cities. That long shared history has created an unbreakable bond and a deep, intuitive understanding of each other.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60453","text":"I would say we have a good balance. We make a point to schedule proper outings, like trying a new restaurant or going to an exhibition, a couple of times a month. But we also value simpler, more frequent interactions, like a quick coffee or a phone call, which are just as important for maintaining our connection.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60454","text":"I appreciate both dynamics for different reasons. One-on-one time allows for deeper, more intimate and vulnerable conversations. Group settings, however, are fantastic for energy, laughter, and shared experiences. I don't have a strong preference; it depends entirely on my mood and what I'm seeking from the social interaction.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60455","text":"They are utterly vital. My friends are my chosen family; they provide a crucial support system, emotional sustenance, and shared joy. They offer different perspectives, honest advice, and unconditional support through life's challenges, making the good times better and the hard times easier to bear.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60456","text":"There's a significant difference. In our teens and early twenties, we almost exclusively met in public places like shopping malls, cinemas, or fast-food restaurants. Now, as adults, we gravitate much more towards each other's homes for dinner, or quieter cafés and pubs where we can actually hear each other talk.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60457","text":"Our activities are quite varied. We often go out for meals or coffee to catch up, go for walks in the park, or watch films together. Sometimes, our meetups are even more low-key—just spending an evening cooking dinner together and talking at home is just as enjoyable.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60458","text":"We tend to favour casual, comfortable environments where we can talk without shouting. Our most common meeting spots are cosy cafés, each other's homes, or parks when the weather is nice. The location is always chosen for its ability to facilitate good conversation.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60459","text":"Suitability hinges on the desired interaction. A noisy sports bar is perfect for watching a match with a group but terrible for a heart-to-heart conversation. A library is suitable for studying together but not for a celebratory party. The ideal venue matches the group's size and the primary goal of the meeting, be it lively socialising or intimate talking.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60460","text":"Absolutely. I consider it the highest form of hospitality and intimacy. Inviting someone into your personal space is a sign of trust and comfort. Some of my best memories with friends are of informal gatherings at home, cooking together, playing games, and talking for hours without the time constraints of a public venue.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Friends&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8310&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-8269","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Advertisement","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"5 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Advertisement</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-60249","sourceQuestionId":60249,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you like advertisements?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60250","sourceQuestionId":60250,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you often see advertisements when you are on your phone or computer?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60251","sourceQuestionId":60251,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you see a lot of advertising on trains or other transport？"},{"id":"igopx-question-60252","sourceQuestionId":60252,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Is there an advertisement that made an impression on you when you were a child?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60253","sourceQuestionId":60253,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"What kind of advertising do you like?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["分别准备你看到广告的渠道和一个具体广告。谈影响时区分吸引注意与真正购买。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60249","approach":"先表达偏好，再解释选择标准；可以补一句例外。","example_direction":["I appreciate well-crafted, creative advertisements that tell a story or are artistically executed.","However, I have a strong aversion to intrusive, repetitive, or blatantly manipulative ads."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60250","approach":"先给频率，再补一项真实活动或原因。","example_direction":["Yes, I frequently encounter advertisements while using my phone or computer.","In fact, digital ads are almost unavoidable in China, appearing on social media platforms, within apps, and as pre-roll videos."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60251","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["An enormous amount.","Public transport is a prime advertising real estate because it captures a captive audience with little else to do during their commute."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60252","approach":"回忆一个具体童年情境，用过去时说明发生了什么以及为何记得。","example_direction":["Yes, I vividly remember a series of animated commercials for a breakfast cereal.","They featured a catchy jingle and a colourful cartoon mascot going on adventures."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60253","approach":"先表达偏好，再解释选择标准；可以补一句例外。","example_direction":["I'm most drawn to minimalist, witty, or emotionally intelligent advertising.","A clever print ad that uses a play on words or a short film-style ad that tells a genuine story without hard-selling a product stands out."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60249","text":"I appreciate well-crafted, creative advertisements that tell a story or are artistically executed. However, I have a strong aversion to intrusive, repetitive, or blatantly manipulative ads. The sheer volume of advertising we are exposed to daily is overwhelming, so the ones that earn my attention are those that offer something of value—be it humour, beauty, or useful information.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60250","text":"Yes, I frequently encounter advertisements while using my phone or computer. In fact, digital ads are almost unavoidable in China, appearing on social media platforms, within apps, and as pre-roll videos. While some can be intrusive, I find many useful, especially those tailored to my interests, as they often introduce me to new products or services I might genuinely like.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60251","text":"An enormous amount. Public transport is a prime advertising real estate because it captures a captive audience with little else to do during their commute. The interiors and exteriors of buses and trains, as well as stations themselves, are plastered with posters and digital screens promoting everything from new movies to university degrees.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60252","text":"Yes, I vividly remember a series of animated commercials for a breakfast cereal. They featured a catchy jingle and a colourful cartoon mascot going on adventures. The combination of bright animation, music, and the promise of a free toy inside made it incredibly memorable and effective on my childhood self.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60253","text":"I'm most drawn to minimalist, witty, or emotionally intelligent advertising. A clever print ad that uses a play on words or a short film-style ad that tells a genuine story without hard-selling a product stands out. I dislike loud, aggressive sales pitches; I prefer ads that respect the audience's intelligence and seek to engage rather than just shout at them.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Advertisement&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8269&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-8375","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Shoes","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"4 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Shoes</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-60779","sourceQuestionId":60779,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you like buying shoes? How often?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60780","sourceQuestionId":60780,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Have you ever bought shoes online?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60781","sourceQuestionId":60781,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"How much money do you usually spend on shoes?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60782","sourceQuestionId":60782,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Which do you prefer, fashionable shoes or comfortable shoes?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["用最近买鞋的经历说明舒适、款式或价格的取舍。过去购买经历用过去时。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60779","approach":"先给频率，再补一项真实活动或原因。","example_direction":["I do, but I’m a considered shopper rather than an impulsive one.","I probably add a new pair to my wardrobe every eight to twelve months, usually to replace a worn-out staple or for a specific purpose, like a new pair of running trainers."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60780","approach":"先明确是否有过，再用过去时说一次简短经历；没有也可说明类似情况。","example_direction":["I have, but I approach it with caution.","I tend to only buy from brands whose sizing I'm already familiar with, or from retailers with a very clear and free returns policy."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60781","approach":"先给大致金额或范围，再说明哪些因素会影响花费。","example_direction":["It varies dramatically depending on the purpose.","I’m happy to spend a significant amount on a high-quality, versatile pair of leather boots or professional shoes that will last for years."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60782","approach":"先表达偏好，再解释选择标准；可以补一句例外。","example_direction":["Comfort wins without question.","I firmly believe there’s no need for these to be mutually exclusive, as many brands now successfully merge style with ergonomics."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60779","text":"I do, but I’m a considered shopper rather than an impulsive one. I probably add a new pair to my wardrobe every eight to twelve months, usually to replace a worn-out staple or for a specific purpose, like a new pair of running trainers. I see them as a functional investment rather than a frequent fashion purchase.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60780","text":"I have, but I approach it with caution. I tend to only buy from brands whose sizing I'm already familiar with, or from retailers with a very clear and free returns policy. The inability to try them on for comfort and fit is a significant drawback, so it requires a bit of research and a leap of faith.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60781","text":"It varies dramatically depending on the purpose. I’m happy to spend a significant amount on a high-quality, versatile pair of leather boots or professional shoes that will last for years. For casual summer footwear like sandals, I’m much more budget-conscious. On average, I’d say I spend a moderate amount, prioritising value over price.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60782","text":"Comfort wins without question. I firmly believe there’s no need for these to be mutually exclusive, as many brands now successfully merge style with ergonomics. However, if forced to choose, I’d always opt for comfort. There’s little point in wearing stylish shoes if you’re in too much pain to enjoy yourself or walk confidently.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Shoes&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8375&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-8349","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Names","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"4 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Names</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71140","sourceQuestionId":71140,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Is it easy to remember people's names?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71141","sourceQuestionId":71141,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"How do you remember people's names?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71142","sourceQuestionId":71142,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"How do you feel when people can't remember your name?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71143","sourceQuestionId":71143,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you often forget people's names?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["本组讨论记住姓名的方法与忘记姓名时的感受。准备一种记忆方法，如重复姓名或关联见面场景，并说一次忘记姓名的经历。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71140","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Honestly, it's not very easy for me.","I often remember faces but forget names."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71141","approach":"先说明一个具体方法或过程，再用日常场景展示怎样实施。","example_direction":["I usually repeat the person's name immediately after hearing it and try to use it in conversation.","I also associate the name with a facial feature or a scene."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71142","approach":"先描述感受，再解释原因或一个具体场景，不把感受题答成时间题。","example_direction":["I would feel a little awkward or disappointed, especially if we've met more than once.","It might seem like I didn't leave an impression."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71143","approach":"先给频率，再补一项真实活动或原因。","example_direction":["Yes, I often forget people's names, especially when I meet them for the first time.","I might remember the face clearly but the name just disappears."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71140","text":"Honestly, it's not very easy for me. I often remember faces but forget names. Especially when I meet several new people at once, their names just slip away. I think names are abstract and don't stick without repetition.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71141","text":"I usually repeat the person's name immediately after hearing it and try to use it in conversation. I also associate the name with a facial feature or a scene. Sometimes I save it in my phone with a small note.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71142","text":"I would feel a little awkward or disappointed, especially if we've met more than once. It might seem like I didn't leave an impression. But I also understand, because I forget names too. So I usually just smile and reintroduce myself.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71143","text":"Yes, I often forget people's names, especially when I meet them for the first time. I might remember the face clearly but the name just disappears. I think it's because I'm not paying full attention during introductions.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Names&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8349&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-8290","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Collecting things","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"4 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Collecting things</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-60354","sourceQuestionId":60354,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you collect things?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60355","sourceQuestionId":60355,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Where do you usually keep things you need?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60356","sourceQuestionId":60356,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Would you keep old things for a long time? Why?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60357","sourceQuestionId":60357,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Are there any things you have kept from your childhood?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选一个真实收藏，如书签或纪念票。说清开始时间、收藏原因和如何存放。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60354","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Yes, I do enjoy collecting things as a hobby.","My collection mainly consists of vintage stamps and coins."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60355","approach":"先给具体地点，再说明选择这个地点的原因或一个相关场景。","example_direction":["I usually keep things I need in an organized manner at home.","Essential items like keys, wallet, and documents have designated places, making them easily accessible."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60356","approach":"先给直接理由，再用一个日常细节说明；无需长篇背景。","example_direction":["Yes, I believe in keeping old things for a long time, especially if they hold sentimental value or have historical significance.","These items serve as tangible connections to the past, preserving memories and stories."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60357","approach":"回忆一个具体童年情境，用过去时说明发生了什么以及为何记得。","example_direction":["Yes, I’ve kept a few toys and books from my childhood that hold special memories.","These items remind me of the carefree days and the joy I experienced while playing and reading."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60354","text":"Yes, I do enjoy collecting things as a hobby. My collection mainly consists of vintage stamps and coins. I find joy in exploring the history and cultural significance behind each item. Collecting allows me to appreciate the diversity of cultures and the artistry of different time periods. It's a fascinating and educational pastime that brings a sense of fulfillment to my leisure activities.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60355","text":"I usually keep things I need in an organized manner at home. Essential items like keys, wallet, and documents have designated places, making them easily accessible. For work-related materials, I maintain a well-organized workspace. Utilizing storage solutions and maintaining a clutter-free environment helps ensure that I can quickly locate and retrieve items when needed.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60356","text":"Yes, I believe in keeping old things for a long time, especially if they hold sentimental value or have historical significance. These items serve as tangible connections to the past, preserving memories and stories. Whether it's family heirlooms, vintage items, or meaningful gifts, holding onto them allows me to appreciate the continuity of life and the value of preserving personal and cultural history.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60357","text":"Yes, I’ve kept a few toys and books from my childhood that hold special memories. These items remind me of the carefree days and the joy I experienced while playing and reading. They serve as nostalgic keepsakes that I cherish and occasionally look back on to reflect on my past.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Collecting%20things&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8290&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-8306","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Feeling bored","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"4 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Feeling bored</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-60428","sourceQuestionId":60428,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you often feel bored?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60429","sourceQuestionId":60429,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you think childhood is boring or adulthood is boring?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60430","sourceQuestionId":60430,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"What do you do when you feel bored?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60431","sourceQuestionId":60431,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"When would you feel bored?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["准备一个感到无聊的场景，以及如何转移注意力。避免把 bored 和 boring 混用。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60428","approach":"先给频率，再补一项真实活动或原因。","example_direction":["No, I don't often feel bored.","I believe in keeping myself engaged and finding activities that interest me."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60429","approach":"按同一标准比较童年和成年生活，再用个人体验解释你的判断。","example_direction":["I think both childhood and adulthood have their own unique aspects, and whether one finds them boring depends on individual perspectives.","In childhood, there's often a sense of innocence and wonder, with plenty of time for play and exploration."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60430","approach":"先说你会采取的行动，再补一个实际例子或解释它如何帮助你。","example_direction":["When I feel bored, I usually try to make the most of that time by engaging in activities that interest me.","One of my favorite things to do is to read books, especially those in genres like science fiction or mystery."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60431","approach":"先给时间，再补一项真实活动或背景。","example_direction":["I usually find myself feeling bored when I'm not mentally stimulated or when I have a lot of free time with nothing specific to do.","For example, during long waits or when there's a lack of interesting activities, I might start to feel a bit bored."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60428","text":"No, I don't often feel bored. I believe in keeping myself engaged and finding activities that interest me. Whether it's pursuing a hobby, reading, or spending time with friends and family, I always try to make the most of my time. I think there's so much to explore and learn in the world, and staying curious helps me avoid boredom. Additionally, I like to set personal goals, which gives me a sense of purpose and keeps me motivated.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60429","text":"I think both childhood and adulthood have their own unique aspects, and whether one finds them boring depends on individual perspectives. In childhood, there's often a sense of innocence and wonder, with plenty of time for play and exploration. However, as an adult, there's a different kind of excitement in taking on responsibilities, pursuing personal goals, and experiencing a greater sense of independence. While childhood memories are filled with carefree moments, adulthood offers a variety of opportunities for personal and professional growth.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60430","text":"When I feel bored, I usually try to make the most of that time by engaging in activities that interest me. One of my favorite things to do is to read books, especially those in genres like science fiction or mystery. It allows me to escape into different worlds and stimulates my imagination. Additionally, I enjoy taking up creative projects, such as writing or experimenting with photography. These activities not only keep me occupied but also provide a sense of accomplishment. If the weather is good, I might go for a walk or explore new places, as it adds a refreshing element to my routine.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60431","text":"I usually find myself feeling bored when I'm not mentally stimulated or when I have a lot of free time with nothing specific to do. For example, during long waits or when there's a lack of interesting activities, I might start to feel a bit bored. However, I've learned to combat this by planning my days effectively and filling my free time with activities that I enjoy. Whether it's reading a book, working on a personal project, or engaging in a hobby, staying proactive helps me ward off boredom and make the most of my time.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Feeling%20bored&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8306&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-8293","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Computers/tablets","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"5 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Computers/tablets</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-60367","sourceQuestionId":60367,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"In what conditions would it be difficult for you to use a computer or tablet?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60368","sourceQuestionId":60368,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"In what conditions would you use a computer or tablet?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60369","sourceQuestionId":60369,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"What would your life be like without computers or tablets?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60370","sourceQuestionId":60370,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"When was the first time you used a computer or tablet?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60371","sourceQuestionId":60371,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Would you like to use a computer or tablet?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["说明设备主要用途，如学习、工作或娱乐。比较电脑和平板时选一项实际体验。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60367","approach":"描述一种具体情境，再说明为什么这种条件影响你的选择或使用体验。","example_direction":["The most obvious condition would be in areas with no internet connectivity or power source, rendering them useless.","It would also be very difficult to use one effectively in a very crowded or bumpy environment, like on a packed train."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60368","approach":"描述一种具体情境，再说明为什么这种条件影响你的选择或使用体验。","example_direction":["I primarily use a computer for complex, focused work that requires multitasking between several windows.","I opt for my tablet in more relaxed settings, like when I'm travelling or want to look up a recipe quickly in the kitchen."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60369","approach":"给一个具体设想，说明条件与原因，避免把未发生的事说成已发生。","example_direction":["It would be profoundly different and considerably more challenging.","My productivity at work would plummet, and staying in touch with friends and family abroad would become much more difficult and slower without instant messaging and video calls."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60370","approach":"先给时间，再补一项真实活动或背景。","example_direction":["I first used a desktop computer in primary school, around the age of seven or eight.","It was a very basic model used for simple educational games and learning to type, which felt incredibly advanced at the time."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60371","approach":"给一个具体设想，说明条件与原因，避免把未发生的事说成已发生。","example_direction":["Definitely.","I find a computer indispensable for serious work tasks like writing reports or analysing data due to the larger screen and full keyboard."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60367","text":"The most obvious condition would be in areas with no internet connectivity or power source, rendering them useless. It would also be very difficult to use one effectively in a very crowded or bumpy environment, like on a packed train.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60368","text":"I primarily use a computer for complex, focused work that requires multitasking between several windows. I opt for my tablet in more relaxed settings, like when I'm travelling or want to look up a recipe quickly in the kitchen.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60369","text":"It would be profoundly different and considerably more challenging. My productivity at work would plummet, and staying in touch with friends and family abroad would become much more difficult and slower without instant messaging and video calls.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60370","text":"I first used a desktop computer in primary school, around the age of seven or eight. It was a very basic model used for simple educational games and learning to type, which felt incredibly advanced at the time.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60371","text":"Definitely. I find a computer indispensable for serious work tasks like writing reports or analysing data due to the larger screen and full keyboard. A tablet is my go-to device for casual browsing, reading, or watching videos on the couch.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Computers%2Ftablets&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8293&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-8337","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Lost and found","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"4 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Lost and found</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-60589","sourceQuestionId":60589,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you report to the police when finding something lost by others? Why?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60590","sourceQuestionId":60590,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Have you ever lost things?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60591","sourceQuestionId":60591,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"What will you do if you find something lost by others?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60592","sourceQuestionId":60592,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Will you post on social media if you lose your item?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["用一次遗失或拾到物品的经历回答。讲清物品、地点和归还或寻找方式。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60589","approach":"先给直接理由，再用一个日常细节说明；无需长篇背景。","example_direction":["I typically wouldn’t report an item to the police unless it’s something very valuable or important, like a wallet or a phone.","For smaller items, I’d prefer to try to find the owner directly or take them to a lost-and-found."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60590","approach":"先明确是否有过，再用过去时说一次简短经历；没有也可说明类似情况。","example_direction":["Yes, I have lost things before, like my keys or my phone on a few occasions.","It can be quite frustrating, especially when I’m in a hurry and can’t find them."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60591","approach":"给一个具体设想，说明条件与原因，避免把未发生的事说成已发生。","example_direction":["If I find something lost by others, I would first try to locate the owner by asking people nearby if they recognize it.","If I can’t find anyone who claims it, I would take it to a lost-and-found area if I’m in a public place."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60592","approach":"给一个具体设想，说明条件与原因，避免把未发生的事说成已发生。","example_direction":["Yes, I might consider posting on social media if I lose something important and cannot find it.","Sharing a post can quickly reach a wider audience, and friends or acquaintances who see it may help me locate the item."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60589","text":"I typically wouldn’t report an item to the police unless it’s something very valuable or important, like a wallet or a phone. For smaller items, I’d prefer to try to find the owner directly or take them to a lost-and-found. Reporting to the police seems more appropriate for significant or sensitive items, as it may require official documentation.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60590","text":"Yes, I have lost things before, like my keys or my phone on a few occasions. It can be quite frustrating, especially when I’m in a hurry and can’t find them. However, I try to stay calm and retrace my steps to locate the lost items.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60591","text":"If I find something lost by others, I would first try to locate the owner by asking people nearby if they recognize it. If I can’t find anyone who claims it, I would take it to a lost-and-found area if I’m in a public place. I believe it’s important to help return lost items to their rightful owners whenever possible.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60592","text":"Yes, I might consider posting on social media if I lose something important and cannot find it. Sharing a post can quickly reach a wider audience, and friends or acquaintances who see it may help me locate the item. It’s a practical way to spread the word, especially if I lost it in a public place.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Lost%20and%20found&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8337&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-8786","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Travelling","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"2 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Travelling</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71138","sourceQuestionId":71138,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you prefer to sit by the window when travelling?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71139","sourceQuestionId":71139,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Did you have a long journey with your family as a child?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["准备靠窗座位的偏好与理由，再回忆一次童年和家人的长途旅行，说明交通方式和印象。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71138","approach":"先表达偏好，再解释选择标准；可以补一句例外。","example_direction":["Yes, I always prefer a window seat when travelling.","I love watching the scenery pass by."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71139","approach":"先明确是否有过，再用过去时说一次简短经历；没有也可说明类似情况。","example_direction":["Yes, I remember taking a very long road trip with my family when I was around eight.","We drove from our city to my grandparents' hometown, which took about twelve hours."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71138","text":"Yes, I always prefer a window seat when travelling. I love watching the scenery pass by. It makes the journey feel more interesting and less boring. If I'm on a plane, I also like seeing the clouds and the city below.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71139","text":"Yes, I remember taking a very long road trip with my family when I was around eight. We drove from our city to my grandparents' hometown, which took about twelve hours. I felt tired and carsick, but my parents made it fun with snacks and music. It's a warm memory now.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Travelling&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8786&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-9827","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Street market","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"4 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Street market</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71144","sourceQuestionId":71144,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"What do people usually buy on the street market?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71145","sourceQuestionId":71145,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you prefer to go shopping in the shopping mall or on the street market?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71146","sourceQuestionId":71146,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"When was the last time you went to a street market?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71147","sourceQuestionId":71147,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Are there many street markets in China?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["描述熟悉的街市和常买的东西。用价格、气氛和交流体验解释喜欢或不喜欢。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71144","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["People usually buy fresh fruits, vegetables, and local snacks at street markets.","You can also find cheap household items, clothes, and sometimes handmade crafts."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71145","approach":"先表达偏好，再解释选择标准；可以补一句例外。","example_direction":["I generally prefer street markets for daily food because it's lively and cheap.","But for buying clothes, electronics, or when the weather is bad, I prefer shopping malls."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71146","approach":"先给时间，再补一项真实活动或背景。","example_direction":["The last time I went to a street market was last Saturday morning.","I went to the morning market near my home to buy some fruit and freshly made soy milk for breakfast."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71147","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Yes, there are many street markets in China.","Almost every neighbourhood has a morning market or a wet market."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71144","text":"People usually buy fresh fruits, vegetables, and local snacks at street markets. You can also find cheap household items, clothes, and sometimes handmade crafts. It's a great place to experience local life and bargain for a good price.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71145","text":"I generally prefer street markets for daily food because it's lively and cheap. But for buying clothes, electronics, or when the weather is bad, I prefer shopping malls. Malls are more comfortable and have better after-sales service. So it really depends on what I need.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71146","text":"The last time I went to a street market was last Saturday morning. I went to the morning market near my home to buy some fruit and freshly made soy milk for breakfast. The place was crowded and full of energy.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71147","text":"Yes, there are many street markets in China. Almost every neighbourhood has a morning market or a wet market. Night markets are also very common, especially in southern cities. They are an important part of daily life and local food culture.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Street%20market&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9827&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-9828","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Politeness","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"2 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Politeness</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71148","sourceQuestionId":71148,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"How did you learn to be polite as a child?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71149","sourceQuestionId":71149,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you think being polite is very important?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["说明童年通过家长示范或学校规则学习礼貌，再用道谢、排队或耐心倾听解释礼貌为何重要。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71148","approach":"说明过去采用的方法或学习过程，再补一个具体回忆，用过去时表达。","example_direction":["I learned to be polite mainly from my parents.","They always reminded me to say 'thank you' and 'please'."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71149","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Yes, politeness is extremely important.","It shows respect for others and helps create a harmonious environment."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71148","text":"I learned to be polite mainly from my parents. They always reminded me to say 'thank you' and 'please'. I also learned from teachers at school. Watching how polite adults behaved around me was probably the biggest influence.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71149","text":"Yes, politeness is extremely important. It shows respect for others and helps create a harmonious environment. Polite people are more likely to be trusted and welcomed. Being polite is the most basic social lubricant; it costs nothing but means a lot.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Politeness&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9828&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-9829","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Tiredness","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"3 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Tiredness</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71150","sourceQuestionId":71150,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you often feel tired?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71151","sourceQuestionId":71151,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"When would you feel tired?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71152","sourceQuestionId":71152,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"What do you do when you feel tired?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["准备容易疲倦的时间段和一种个人恢复方式。用一段学习或工作后的实际感受让回答具体。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71150","approach":"先给频率，再补一项真实活动或原因。","example_direction":["Yes, I often feel tired, especially after a long day of work or study.","Sometimes even after waking up, I still feel exhausted."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71151","approach":"先给时间，再补一项真实活动或背景。","example_direction":["I usually feel tired in the late afternoon, around three or four o'clock.","After lunch, my energy drops and I feel sleepy."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71152","approach":"先说你会采取的行动，再补一个实际例子或解释它如何帮助你。","example_direction":["When I feel tired, I usually take a short nap or drink a cup of coffee.","Sometimes I go for a quick walk to refresh my mind."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71150","text":"Yes, I often feel tired, especially after a long day of work or study. Sometimes even after waking up, I still feel exhausted. I think it's a combination of physical fatigue and mental stress.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71151","text":"I usually feel tired in the late afternoon, around three or four o'clock. After lunch, my energy drops and I feel sleepy. Also, after finishing a mentally intense task, I feel drained. Long commutes in the evening make it worse.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71152","text":"When I feel tired, I usually take a short nap or drink a cup of coffee. Sometimes I go for a quick walk to refresh my mind. If I'm at home, I might listen to some soft music or take a warm shower. The key is to stop and give myself a break.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Tiredness&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9829&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-9830","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Rubbish and recycling","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"4 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Rubbish and recycling</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71153","sourceQuestionId":71153,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"What do you do when you see rubbish on the street?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71154","sourceQuestionId":71154,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"How do you recycle things like paper and plastic?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71155","sourceQuestionId":71155,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Is waste sorting common in your country?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71156","sourceQuestionId":71156,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Did you recycle when you were a kid?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["说清家中垃圾分类或回收习惯。没有完善设施时如实说明具体困难。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71153","approach":"先说你会采取的行动，再补一个实际例子或解释它如何帮助你。","example_direction":["I usually pick it up if it's not too dirty and throw it into a nearby bin.","If I see someone littering, I might give a polite reminder."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71154","approach":"先说明一个具体方法或过程，再用日常场景展示怎样实施。","example_direction":["I separate paper, plastic, and glass at home into different bins.","Our community has designated recycling stations."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71155","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["es, waste sorting is becoming more and more common in China.","Many cities now require residents to separate kitchen waste, recyclables, hazardous waste, and other waste."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71156","approach":"先明确是否有过，再用过去时说一次简短经历；没有也可说明类似情况。","example_direction":["Not really.","When I was a kid, waste sorting wasn't widely promoted."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71153","text":"I usually pick it up if it's not too dirty and throw it into a nearby bin. If I see someone littering, I might give a polite reminder. I believe keeping streets clean is everyone's responsibility. Small actions can make a big difference.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71154","text":"I separate paper, plastic, and glass at home into different bins. Our community has designated recycling stations. I also reuse plastic bags and donate old books to charity. I try to reduce waste first, then recycle what's left.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71155","text":"es, waste sorting is becoming more and more common in China. Many cities now require residents to separate kitchen waste, recyclables, hazardous waste, and other waste. There are sorting stations in communities and volunteers to guide people. It's a national trend, though enforcement varies.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71156","text":"Not really. When I was a kid, waste sorting wasn't widely promoted. We only separated recyclable paper and bottles sometimes because we could sell them for pocket money. Most household waste went into one bin. The awareness came later.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Rubbish%20and%20recycling&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9830&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-9831","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Paper","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"5 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Paper</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71157","sourceQuestionId":71157,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Have you made any crafts with paper?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71158","sourceQuestionId":71158,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you still write physical letters?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71159","sourceQuestionId":71159,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do people still keep handwritten letters today?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71160","sourceQuestionId":71160,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you carry paper and pens with you when you go out?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71161","sourceQuestionId":71161,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"What did you like to do with paper as a child?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["本组涉及纸艺、书信和随身纸笔。准备一种童年纸艺与现在写纸质信的习惯，区分过去经历和当前用途。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71157","approach":"先明确是否有过，再用过去时说一次简短经历；没有也可说明类似情况。","example_direction":["Yes, I used to make paper planes and origami cranes when I was a child.","At school, we would fold paper frogs and race them on the desk."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71158","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["I rarely write physical letters now.","The last time I wrote one was to my grandmother, because she doesn't use a smartphone."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71159","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Some people do keep them, especially older generations.","Handwritten letters carry emotional value."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71160","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["I usually carry a small notebook and a pen in my bag.","But I rarely use them because everything is on my phone."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71161","approach":"先描述过去做过的具体活动，再补一项细节或原因。","example_direction":["As a child, I loved drawing on paper.","I would fill every corner with doodles."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71157","text":"Yes, I used to make paper planes and origami cranes when I was a child. At school, we would fold paper frogs and race them on the desk. Last year, I also made a simple paper lantern for a festival. It's a cheap and fun way to create something.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71158","text":"I rarely write physical letters now. The last time I wrote one was to my grandmother, because she doesn't use a smartphone. I think handwritten letters feel more personal and precious, but they take too much time. So I usually send messages or emails instead.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71159","text":"Some people do keep them, especially older generations. Handwritten letters carry emotional value. They are seen as keepsakes of important times. However, among young people, it is rare. Most letters exist digitally now, as screenshots or saved messages.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71160","text":"I usually carry a small notebook and a pen in my bag. But I rarely use them because everything is on my phone. Still, I feel safer having them in case I need to jot down something quickly or my phone dies.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71161","text":"As a child, I loved drawing on paper. I would fill every corner with doodles. I also enjoyed folding paper planes and boats. Cutting paper into snowflakes was my favourite winter activity. Paper was my first creative toy.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Paper&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9831&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-9832","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Fruit and vegetables","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"5 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Fruit and vegetables</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71162","sourceQuestionId":71162,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"How often do you eat fruit and vegetables?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71163","sourceQuestionId":71163,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Where do you usually buy fruit and vegetables?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71164","sourceQuestionId":71164,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"What kind of fruits and vegetables do you dislike?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71165","sourceQuestionId":71165,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Were there any kinds of fruits and vegetables you disliked as a child?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71166","sourceQuestionId":71166,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do people in your country like planting vegetables?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["准备常吃的一种水果和一种蔬菜。用口味、季节或做法让回答具体。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71162","approach":"先给频率，再补一项真实活动或原因。","example_direction":["I eat fruit and vegetables every day.","I try to have at least one apple or banana, and vegetables with lunch and dinner."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71163","approach":"先给具体地点，再说明选择这个地点的原因或一个相关场景。","example_direction":["I usually buy fruit and vegetables at the local wet market or the supermarket near my home.","The wet market has fresher and cheaper produce."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71164","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["I dislike bitter melon the most.","Its strong bitter taste is hard for me to accept."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71165","approach":"回忆一个具体童年情境，用过去时说明发生了什么以及为何记得。","example_direction":["Yes, as a child I hated coriander and carrots.","My mum had to chop them into tiny pieces and hide them in dumplings."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71166","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Yes, many people in China like planting vegetables, especially the older generation.","They grow them on balconies, roofs, or small patches of land."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71162","text":"I eat fruit and vegetables every day. I try to have at least one apple or banana, and vegetables with lunch and dinner. My mother always insisted on this habit. Eating them keeps my digestion good and my skin clear.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71163","text":"I usually buy fruit and vegetables at the local wet market or the supermarket near my home. The wet market has fresher and cheaper produce. Sometimes I order from a grocery app if I'm busy.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71164","text":"I dislike bitter melon the most. Its strong bitter taste is hard for me to accept. I also avoid celery because of its stringy texture. Other than that, I enjoy most common vegetables and fruits.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71165","text":"Yes, as a child I hated coriander and carrots. My mum had to chop them into tiny pieces and hide them in dumplings. I've gradually accepted them now. But the childhood aversion was very strong.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71166","text":"Yes, many people in China like planting vegetables, especially the older generation. They grow them on balconies, roofs, or small patches of land. It is partly a habit from rural life and partly for health and saving money. Even some young people are joining this trend.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Fruit%20and%20vegetables&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9832&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-9833","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Secondary school","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"4 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Secondary school</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71167","sourceQuestionId":71167,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you remember your first day at secondary school?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71168","sourceQuestionId":71168,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Were there any subjects that you found difficult at secondary school?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71169","sourceQuestionId":71169,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"What was your favorite subject at secondary school?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71170","sourceQuestionId":71170,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Is there anything you miss about your secondary school?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["准备中学的一门课、一位老师和一次难忘活动。回忆经历用过去时。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71167","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Yes, I remember it very clearly.","I was both excited and nervous."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71168","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Yes, maths was quite difficult for me.","Especially geometry and functions."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71169","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["My favourite subject was English.","I loved learning new words and watching English movies in class."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71170","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Yes, I miss the simple friendship and the carefree days.","Everyone was so pure and full of dreams."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71167","text":"Yes, I remember it very clearly. I was both excited and nervous. The school was much bigger than my primary school. I got lost trying to find my classroom. But my form teacher was kind, and I made a friend on the first day.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71168","text":"Yes, maths was quite difficult for me. Especially geometry and functions. I often couldn't understand the logic, and the pace of the class was fast. I had to spend extra time on practice problems just to keep up.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71169","text":"My favourite subject was English. I loved learning new words and watching English movies in class. The teacher made lessons fun with games and songs. I felt a sense of achievement when I could express myself in another language.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71170","text":"Yes, I miss the simple friendship and the carefree days. Everyone was so pure and full of dreams. I also miss the canteen food and the little shops near the school gate. Those were the best times of my youth.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Secondary%20school&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9833&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-8345","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Morning routines「邪21」","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"4 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Morning routines「邪21」</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-60629","sourceQuestionId":60629,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you like to get up early in the morning?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60631","sourceQuestionId":60631,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"What do you do right after getting up in the morning?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60630","sourceQuestionId":60630,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Is breakfast important?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60632","sourceQuestionId":60632,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"What is your morning routine?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["按起床、早餐和出门的顺序说明早晨习惯，再比较工作日与周末。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60629","approach":"先表达偏好，再解释选择标准；可以补一句例外。","example_direction":["Yes, I prefer getting up early in the morning as it allows me to kickstart my day with a sense of productivity.","The quietude of the early hours provides me with a peaceful environment to engage in activities like exercise, meditation, and planning, setting a positive tone for the day ahead."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60631","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Right after I wake up, I like to take a few moments to stretch and gather my thoughts for the day.","Then, I brush my teeth and wash my face to feel refreshed."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60630","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Yes, breakfast is crucial for starting the day right.","It provides essential nutrients and energy to kickstart metabolism after a night of fasting."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60632","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["My morning routine begins with waking up at 6:30 a.m.","followed by some stretching exercises to invigorate my body."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60629","text":"Yes, I prefer getting up early in the morning as it allows me to kickstart my day with a sense of productivity. The quietude of the early hours provides me with a peaceful environment to engage in activities like exercise, meditation, and planning, setting a positive tone for the day ahead.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60631","text":"Right after I wake up, I like to take a few moments to stretch and gather my thoughts for the day. Then, I brush my teeth and wash my face to feel refreshed. After that, I enjoy a healthy breakfast, usually something like oatmeal or fruit, which gives me energy for the day ahead.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60630","text":"Yes, breakfast is crucial for starting the day right. It provides essential nutrients and energy to kickstart metabolism after a night of fasting. Studies show that people who eat breakfast tend to have better concentration, mood, and overall health compared to those who skip it.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60632","text":"My morning routine begins with waking up at 6:30 a.m. followed by some stretching exercises to invigorate my body. Afterward, I enjoy a nutritious breakfast consisting of oats and fruits. Then, I review my schedule for the day and prepare for work or study, ensuring a productive start.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Morning%20routines%E3%80%8C%E9%82%AA21%E3%80%8D&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8345&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-8271","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Art「邪21」","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"4 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Art「邪21」</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-60263","sourceQuestionId":60263,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you like art?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60267","sourceQuestionId":60267,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you like visiting art galleries?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60268","sourceQuestionId":60268,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you want to be an artist?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60265","sourceQuestionId":60265,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you like modern art or traditional art?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选一种接触过的艺术，如音乐、绘画或展览。即使不擅长，也可以解释欣赏方式。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60263","approach":"先表达偏好，再解释选择标准；可以补一句例外。","example_direction":["Yes, I'm a real enthusiast.","I don't just mean paintings; I appreciate a wide spectrum, from sculpture and photography to digital installations."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60267","approach":"先表达偏好，再解释选择标准；可以补一句例外。","example_direction":["Absolutely.","I find it a profoundly enriching experience."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60268","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["While I have immense admiration for artists, I don't think it's the right path for me.","I lack the technical skill, but more importantly, I see myself as more of an appreciator and patron of the arts rather than a creator."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60265","approach":"先表达偏好，再解释选择标准；可以补一句例外。","example_direction":["I appreciate both for different reasons.","Traditional art amazes me with its technical mastery and historical narrative."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60263","text":"Yes, I'm a real enthusiast. I don't just mean paintings; I appreciate a wide spectrum, from sculpture and photography to digital installations. I find it's a powerful medium for expressing complex emotions and ideas that are sometimes hard to articulate with words alone.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60267","text":"Absolutely. I find it a profoundly enriching experience. It's not just about viewing the art itself, but also about understanding the historical context and the artist's perspective. I always leave feeling inspired and with a broader outlook.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60268","text":"While I have immense admiration for artists, I don't think it's the right path for me. I lack the technical skill, but more importantly, I see myself as more of an appreciator and patron of the arts rather than a creator.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60265","text":"I appreciate both for different reasons. Traditional art amazes me with its technical mastery and historical narrative. Modern art, however, often challenges my perceptions and invites more personal interpretation. I wouldn't say I prefer one over the other.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Art%E3%80%8C%E9%82%AA21%E3%80%8D&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8271&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-8381","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Social media「邪21」","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"5 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Social media「邪21」</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-60805","sourceQuestionId":60805,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you think you spend too much time on social media?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60806","sourceQuestionId":60806,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do your friends use social media?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60807","sourceQuestionId":60807,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"What do people often do on social media?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60808","sourceQuestionId":60808,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"When did you start using social media?"},{"id":"igopx-question-64503","sourceQuestionId":64503,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Have you ever posted anything on social media?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["说一个平台的实际用途和使用频率。讨论限制时举一次分心经历，避免抽象说教。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60805","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["I believe I spend a reasonable amount of time on social media.","While it can be easy to get absorbed, I try to maintain a healthy balance between online and offline activities."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60806","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Yes, the majority of my friends use social media.","It has become a common and convenient way for us to stay connected, especially considering our busy lifestyles."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60807","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["People engage in various activities on social media.","Primarily, they use it to connect with friends and family, sharing updates about their lives through posts and photos."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60808","approach":"先给时间，再补一项真实活动或背景。","example_direction":["I started using social media around the age of 14.","I was curious about connecting with friends and sharing experiences online."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-64503","approach":"先明确是否有过，再用过去时说一次简短经历；没有也可说明类似情况。","example_direction":["Yes, I posted some photos from my trip to Yunnan on WeChat last year.","I don't post often, but when I visit a beautiful place, I like to share the moment with my close friends and family online."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60805","text":"I believe I spend a reasonable amount of time on social media. While it can be easy to get absorbed, I try to maintain a healthy balance between online and offline activities.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60806","text":"Yes, the majority of my friends use social media. It has become a common and convenient way for us to stay connected, especially considering our busy lifestyles. We share updates, photos, and communicate through various platforms. While it's a valuable tool for maintaining friendships, we also recognize the importance of face-to-face interactions and try to balance our online and offline connections.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60807","text":"People engage in various activities on social media. Primarily, they use it to connect with friends and family, sharing updates about their lives through posts and photos. Additionally, social media serves as a platform for information consumption, where people follow news, trends, and content creators. It's common to see discussions and opinions on diverse topics, fostering virtual communities. Some also use social media for entertainment, such as watching videos or participating in online challenges.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60808","text":"I started using social media around the age of 14. I was curious about connecting with friends and sharing experiences online.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-64503","text":"Yes, I posted some photos from my trip to Yunnan on WeChat last year. I don't post often, but when I visit a beautiful place, I like to share the moment with my close friends and family online.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Social%20media%E3%80%8C%E9%82%AA21%E3%80%8D&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8381&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p1-8394","type":"speaking","title":"Part 1 · Teachers「邪21」","book":"口语全集题目","part":1,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":null,"passage":"<h2>Teachers「邪21」</h2><p>Part 1</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-60863","sourceQuestionId":60863,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Are you still in touch with your primary school teachers?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60864","sourceQuestionId":60864,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you have a favorite teacher?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60866","sourceQuestionId":60866,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you have a teacher from your past that you still remember?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60867","sourceQuestionId":60867,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you want to be a teacher in the future?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60868","sourceQuestionId":60868,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"In what way has your favourite teacher helped you?"},{"id":"igopx-question-64881","sourceQuestionId":64881,"type":"speaking","part":1,"text":"Do you like your primary school teachers more than your high school teachers?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["准备一位影响你的老师和一个具体教学行为。用反馈或鼓励说明为何难忘。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60863","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["No, I’m not in touch with my primary school teachers anymore.","Life has moved us in different directions, but I fondly remember their influence and the lessons they taught me."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60864","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Yes, I have a favorite teacher who was incredibly inspiring.","Their passion for the subject and engaging teaching methods made learning enjoyable and significantly influenced my academic and personal growth."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60866","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["Yes, I still remember a teacher from my past who made a significant impact on me.","Their innovative teaching methods and genuine encouragement inspired me and shaped my academic interests."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60867","approach":"给一个具体设想，说明条件与原因，避免把未发生的事说成已发生。","example_direction":["I’m considering becoming a teacher in the future.","I find the idea of guiding and inspiring students appealing, and I believe it could be a fulfilling way to share my knowledge and passion."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60868","approach":"先直接回答，再补原因或一个具体例子，保持简短自然。","example_direction":["My favorite teacher profoundly impacted me by fostering a love for learning and encouraging critical thinking.","Their support and insightful feedback helped me build confidence and excel academically."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-64881","approach":"先表达偏好，再解释选择标准；可以补一句例外。","example_direction":["Yes, I probably do.","My primary school teachers were usually much warmer and more patient, so I felt emotionally closer to them."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60863","text":"No, I’m not in touch with my primary school teachers anymore. Life has moved us in different directions, but I fondly remember their influence and the lessons they taught me.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60864","text":"Yes, I have a favorite teacher who was incredibly inspiring. Their passion for the subject and engaging teaching methods made learning enjoyable and significantly influenced my academic and personal growth.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60866","text":"Yes, I still remember a teacher from my past who made a significant impact on me. Their innovative teaching methods and genuine encouragement inspired me and shaped my academic interests.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60867","text":"I’m considering becoming a teacher in the future. I find the idea of guiding and inspiring students appealing, and I believe it could be a fulfilling way to share my knowledge and passion.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60868","text":"My favorite teacher profoundly impacted me by fostering a love for learning and encouraging critical thinking. Their support and insightful feedback helped me build confidence and excel academically.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-64881","text":"Yes, I probably do. My primary school teachers were usually much warmer and more patient, so I felt emotionally closer to them. Back then, classes were less stressful, and teachers often encouraged us through games and small rewards, which made school feel enjoyable.\nIn high school, although many teachers were professional and responsible, they tended to focus more on exam results and academic pressure. As a result, the relationship between teachers and students felt a bit more distant and serious.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=Teachers%E3%80%8C%E9%82%AA21%E3%80%8D&unitName=part1&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8394&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-8681","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 好的购物服务","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8681,"passage":"<h2>好的购物服务</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-62735","sourceQuestionId":62735,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a time when you received good service in a shop/store\nYou should say:\nWhere the shop is\nWhen you went to the shop\nWhat service you received from the staff\nAnd explain how you felt about the service"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["可用一次买电子产品、修鞋或退换货的经历。突出店员具体做了什么额外帮助。","故事顺序为需求或困难、店员行动、问题解决、你的感受；用一个小细节证明服务好。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62735","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I’d like to talk about an experience I had at a small, independent electronics store in my city.","I went there about a year ago when I was urgently trying to find a specific adapter for my laptop before an important online presentation later that day."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62735","text":"I’d like to talk about an experience I had at a small, independent electronics store in my city. I went there about a year ago when I was urgently trying to find a specific adapter for my laptop before an important online presentation later that day. The shop was quite cramped and unassuming from the outside. The service I received was exceptional. The owner, an older gentleman, noticed I looked stressed and immediately asked how he could help. After I explained what I needed, he didn't just point me to a shelf; he spent a good ten minutes testing different adapters with my laptop to ensure compatibility and optimal power output. He even taught me how to identify the right specifications myself in the future. What truly stood out was that he refused to upsell me a more expensive model, insisting the mid-range one was perfectly adequate for my needs. I felt incredibly valued and relieved. His expertise and genuine desire to help, rather than just make a sale, transformed a stressful errand into a positive experience. It built a great deal of trust, and I’ve been a loyal customer ever since.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%A5%BD%E7%9A%84%E8%B4%AD%E7%89%A9%E6%9C%8D%E5%8A%A1&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8681&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-8702","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 钦佩的运动员","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8702,"passage":"<h2>钦佩的运动员</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-62861","sourceQuestionId":62861,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a successful sportsperson you admire\nYou should say:\nWho he/she is\nWhat you know about him/her\nWhat he/she is like in real life\nWhat achievement he/she has made\nAnd explain why you admire him/her"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选你真正了解的运动员，准备一个训练、比赛或复出的事例。","不要只讲奖项；用面对困难的行为解释钦佩，并联系对你的影响。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62861","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["The successful sportsperson I truly admire is the Chinese badminton legend Lin Dan.","He is widely regarded as one of the greatest singles players of all time, dominating the sport for nearly two decades."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62861","text":"The successful sportsperson I truly admire is the Chinese badminton legend Lin Dan. He is widely regarded as one of the greatest singles players of all time, dominating the sport for nearly two decades. What I know about him extends beyond his athletic prowess; he is known for his fierce competitiveness, incredible agility, and powerful smashes on the court. Off the court, he is often described as charismatic, confident, and somewhat rebellious, which earned him the nickname \"Super Dan.\" His achievements are extraordinary: he is the only player to complete the \"Super Grand Slam\" by winning all nine major titles in the badminton world, including two Olympic gold medals and five World Championships. The reason I admire him so much is not just because of his victories, but because of his mental strength and longevity in such a demanding sport. He consistently performed under pressure, overcame injuries, and maintained his passion and discipline throughout his career, making him a true icon of perseverance and excellence.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E9%92%A6%E4%BD%A9%E7%9A%84%E8%BF%90%E5%8A%A8%E5%91%98&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8702&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-8503","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 嘈杂地","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8503,"passage":"<h2>嘈杂地</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-61561","sourceQuestionId":61561,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a noisy place you have been to\nYou should say:\nWhere it is\nWhen you went there\nWhat you did there\nAnd explain why you feel it's a noisy place"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选市场、车站或施工附近，说明去那里的目的和时间。","用广播、车辆、人群等两种声音营造场景，再说噪声怎样影响你以及你如何应对。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61561","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["One of the most overwhelmingly noisy places I've experienced in China was Beijing's Silk Street Market (Xiushui Market) during peak shopping hours.","I visited this famous shopping destination last winter while showing some visiting relatives around the city."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61561","text":"One of the most overwhelmingly noisy places I've experienced in China was Beijing's Silk Street Market (Xiushui Market) during peak shopping hours. I visited this famous shopping destination last winter while showing some visiting relatives around the city. The moment we stepped inside, we were immediately engulfed in a cacophony of sounds. Vendors were enthusiastically hawking their goods, their voices rising above the general din as they competed for customers' attention. The constant hum of bargaining in multiple languages created a peculiar soundscape - Mandarin, English, Russian, and various dialects all blending together. Adding to this were the sounds of hangers clanging, cash registers beeping, and the occasional loudspeaker announcements about special promotions. We spent about two hours there browsing through counterfeit luxury goods and traditional souvenirs. What struck me most was how the noise levels fluctuated - reaching crescendos when popular stalls had bidding wars over prices, then momentarily subsiding before erupting again. I remember trying to negotiate for a \"North Face\" jacket while simultaneously shouting to be heard over a nearby vendor demonstrating some electronic gadget at full volume. What makes this place exceptionally noisy isn't just the volume, but the layered nature of the sounds. The market's enclosed space with poor acoustics amplifies everything, creating an almost physical wall of noise. Unlike predictable industrial noise, this was chaotic human energy - the sound of commerce and cultural exchange at its most vibrant. While initially overwhelming, I came to appreciate this noise as part of the market's unique character. It represented Beijing's dynamic commercial spirit, though I must admit, we all left with slight headaches and an urgent need for some peaceful tea afterwards!","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%98%88%E6%9D%82%E5%9C%B0&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8503&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-8559","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 想再去一次的城市","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8559,"passage":"<h2>想再去一次的城市</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-61928","sourceQuestionId":61928,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a city that you have been to and would like to visit again.\nYou should say:\nWhen you visited it\nWhat you did there\nWhat it was like\nAnd explain why you would like to visit it again"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选去过的城市，准备一个具体地点和一项还未体验的活动。","先讲第一次到访的经历，再解释想重访的原因与下一次计划，保持时态变化清晰。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61928","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["One Chinese city I deeply admire is Hangzhou, which I visited in autumn 2022.","Known as \"Paradise on Earth,\" it perfectly blends natural beauty, history, and modernity."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61928","text":"One Chinese city I deeply admire is Hangzhou, which I visited in autumn 2022. Known as \"Paradise on Earth,\" it perfectly blends natural beauty, history, and modernity.\nI spent three days there, primarily around West Lake, a popular site where willow trees reflect on misty waters. I rented a bike to cycle the lakeshore, stopping at landmarks like Leifeng Pagoda and the Broken Bridge. A highlight was taking a traditional boat ride at sunset while listening to the guide's legends about ancient poets who immortalized the lake. I also explored Lingyin Temple, marveling at its 1,700-year-old Buddhist rock carvings, and sampled Hangzhou's famous dishes like Dongpo pork and Longjing tea shrimp at a lakeside restaurant.\nHangzhou struck me as harmonious and elegant. The city seamlessly merges skyscrapers with tea plantations—I visited a Longjing tea village in the hills, where farmers taught me to pick tea leaves. Unlike Shanghai's bustle, Hangzhou's pace felt relaxed, with locals practicing tai chi by the lake or sipping tea in bamboo groves.\nI'd return to experience Hangzhou's four seasons. I missed spring, when peach blossoms blanket the lake, and winter's \"Snow on the Broken Bridge\" scene. I'd also explore Xixi Wetland by gondola and attend a tea ceremony at the China National Tea Museum. Hangzhou embodies China's poetic soul, offering timeless tranquility amid rapid urbanization—a rarity I crave to relive.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E6%83%B3%E5%86%8D%E5%8E%BB%E4%B8%80%E6%AC%A1%E7%9A%84%E5%9F%8E%E5%B8%82&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8559&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-8417","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 一见且想再见的人","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8417,"passage":"<h2>一见且想再见的人</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-60984","sourceQuestionId":60984,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a person you only met once recently and want to know more about\nYou should say:\nWho he/she is\nWhen you met him/her\nWhy you want to know more about him/her\nAnd explain how you feel about him/her"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选旅行、课程或活动中只见过一次的人。","描述短暂交谈中的一个细节或共同兴趣，再解释为何希望再次见面，不必编造复杂身份。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60984","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I’d like to talk about a person I met recently at a conference, whom I found particularly intriguing and would love to know more about.","Her name is Dr."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60984","text":"I’d like to talk about a person I met recently at a conference, whom I found particularly intriguing and would love to know more about. Her name is Dr. Li, and she’s a researcher in the field of environmental science. I met her just last month at an academic symposium I attended. She gave a presentation on sustainable urban development, which really piqued my interest. The reason I want to know more about Dr. Li is not just because of her fascinating work, but also because of the way she presents herself. She seemed incredibly passionate about her field and had an engaging and thoughtful approach to complex issues. I had the chance to speak with her briefly after her talk, and her responses were insightful and inspiring. She even shared some of her future research plans, which left me eager to learn more. What particularly impressed me about her was the depth of her knowledge and her ability to explain intricate concepts in such a clear and accessible way. I feel she could provide valuable advice for my own academic journey, especially as I’m looking into similar research areas. I also admire her dedication to promoting environmental sustainability and the practical impact of her work. Overall, I feel both inspired and motivated after meeting Dr. Li. I’d love to stay in touch and perhaps learn from her experiences in the future.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E4%B8%80%E8%A7%81%E4%B8%94%E6%83%B3%E5%86%8D%E8%A7%81%E7%9A%84%E4%BA%BA&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8417&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-8466","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 印象深刻的课程","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8466,"passage":"<h2>印象深刻的课程</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-61323","sourceQuestionId":61323,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a course that impressed you a lot\nYou should say:\nWhat the course was about\nWhere you took the course\nWhat you did during the course\nAnd explain why it impressed you a lot"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选一堂改变认识或让你掌握技能的课。","说明老师的演示、你遇到的困难、如何理解，以及后来怎样用到知识。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61323","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I’d like to talk about a course that left a lasting impression on me – it was a creative writing course I took at my university last semester.","The course was designed to help students improve their writing skills, particularly in fiction and storytelling, which is an area I’ve always been interested in."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61323","text":"I’d like to talk about a course that left a lasting impression on me – it was a creative writing course I took at my university last semester. The course was designed to help students improve their writing skills, particularly in fiction and storytelling, which is an area I’ve always been interested in. I took the course as part of an elective in the literature department. The class was relatively small, which allowed for more personalized attention from the professor. Over the course of several weeks, we explored various writing techniques, from character development to plot structure. We also had the chance to write our own short stories and receive feedback from both the instructor and our peers. One of the most interesting activities was the peer review sessions. We would exchange our work with classmates and critique each other’s stories. This process helped me to see my own writing from a different perspective and to understand how others interpret the same material. What impressed me the most was how the course not only improved my writing skills but also sparked my creativity. The professor encouraged us to experiment with different styles and genres, and this freedom to explore really made me enjoy the process of writing again. By the end of the course, I had gained more confidence in my abilities and developed a deeper appreciation for the art of storytelling.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%8D%B0%E8%B1%A1%E6%B7%B1%E5%88%BB%E7%9A%84%E8%AF%BE%E7%A8%8B&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8466&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-8538","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 帮助他人","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8538,"passage":"<h2>帮助他人</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-61786","sourceQuestionId":61786,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a time when you helped someone\nYou should say:\nWho you helped\nWhy you helped him/her\nHow you helped him/her\nAnd explain how you felt about the experience"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选一次具体帮助，如辅导同学、带路或协助搬家。","用对方困难、你的行动、结果和双方感受组织；帮助程度无需夸大。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61786","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I'd like to share a memorable experience when I helped a friend named Sarah.","Sarah and I have been close friends since childhood, and she's always been there for me in times of need."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61786","text":"I'd like to share a memorable experience when I helped a friend named Sarah. Sarah and I have been close friends since childhood, and she's always been there for me in times of need.\nAbout a year ago, Sarah faced a challenging situation. Her father had fallen seriously ill and was hospitalized for an extended period. The medical bills were piling up, and the family was struggling to manage the financial burden.\nRecognizing her distress, I felt a strong urge to help her. I knew that her father's health was her top priority, and I wanted to alleviate some of the financial stress. So, I organized a fundraising campaign among our friends and acquaintances. We set up an online crowdfunding platform, shared the story of her father's illness, and appealed for contributions.\nThrough the collective efforts of our network, we managed to raise a significant amount of money to ease the financial strain on Sarah's family. It was heartwarming to see the outpouring of support from friends, colleagues, and even strangers who were touched by Sarah's situation.\nAs for how I felt about the experience, it was incredibly rewarding. Knowing that I could make a difference in Sarah's life during such a challenging time brought me a profound sense of fulfillment and strengthened our friendship. It reaffirmed my belief in the power of community and the importance of being there for our friends when they need us the most.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%B8%AE%E5%8A%A9%E4%BB%96%E4%BA%BA&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8538&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-8583","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 拥挤地方","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8583,"passage":"<h2>拥挤地方</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-62088","sourceQuestionId":62088,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a crowded place you went to\nYou should say:\nWhen you went there\nWho you went there with\nWhy you went there\nAnd how you felt about it"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选一次高峰车站、节日商场或景点经历。","解释为何拥挤，再描述移动或交流受影响的一刻；结尾说体验与应对方法。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62088","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I’d like to talk about my visit to a popular music festival that I attended last summer.","The festival took place in a large open field just outside the city, and it attracted thousands of people from all over the region."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62088","text":"I’d like to talk about my visit to a popular music festival that I attended last summer. The festival took place in a large open field just outside the city, and it attracted thousands of people from all over the region. I went there with a group of my close friends, as we were all excited to see some of our favorite bands and artists perform live. It was a much-anticipated event for us, and we had been looking forward to it for months.\nFrom the moment we arrived, the place was packed with people. There were crowds everywhere—at the food stalls, around the stages, and even in the lines for the restrooms. The atmosphere was electric, with music blasting from multiple stages, bright lights, and the buzz of excited conversations. The sheer number of people made it challenging to move around, and at times it felt overwhelming to navigate through the sea of concertgoers.\nDespite the crowd, I thoroughly enjoyed the experience. The energy was contagious, and it was thrilling to be part of such a lively and vibrant gathering. Watching live performances with my friends and singing along with the crowd was an unforgettable experience. Although it was hectic and sometimes chaotic, the excitement and fun of the festival made it all worthwhile.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E6%8B%A5%E6%8C%A4%E5%9C%B0%E6%96%B9&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8583&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-8476","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 受欢迎的人","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8476,"passage":"<h2>受欢迎的人</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-61385","sourceQuestionId":61385,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a popular person\nYou should say:\nWho this person is\nWhat kind of person he or she is\nWhen you see him/her normally\nAnd explain why you think this person is popular"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选身边受欢迎的同学、同事或邻居。","用一个他帮助别人或组织活动的例子证明受欢迎，避免只罗列形容词。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61385","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I would like to talk about Zhong Nanshan, a renowned pulmonologist in China.","He is a highly dedicated and courageous medical professional, widely respected for his integrity and expertise."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61385","text":"I would like to talk about Zhong Nanshan, a renowned pulmonologist in China. He is a highly dedicated and courageous medical professional, widely respected for his integrity and expertise. I normally see him during major public health broadcasts or news conferences, especially during critical times such as the COVID-19 pandemic.\nDr. Zhong rose to national prominence during the SARS outbreak in 2003, where his transparent and decisive actions were instrumental in combating the epidemic. Decades later, he again played a pivotal role during the COVID-19 crisis, providing authoritative guidance and reassuring the public with his scientific approach and empathetic leadership. His commitment to truth and public welfare, despite his advanced age, has made him a symbol of trust and professionalism. Beyond his medical achievements, he maintains a humble and rigorous attitude toward scientific research, inspiring countless young people to pursue careers in medicine and public service. His influence extends beyond healthcare; he represents resilience and moral courage, making him deeply admired across generations in China.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%8F%97%E6%AC%A2%E8%BF%8E%E7%9A%84%E4%BA%BA&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8476&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-8666","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 节约时间的方法/改变","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8666,"passage":"<h2>节约时间的方法/改变</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-62636","sourceQuestionId":62636,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a way/change that helps you save a lot of time\nYou should say:\nWhat it is\nHow you implement it\nHow difficult it is\nAnd explain how you feel about the way/change"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选一个实际改变，如提前准备衣物、批量做饭或使用日历。","对比改变前后的具体流程和节省的时间，再解释新方法是否有局限。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62636","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["A significant change that has helped me save a lot of time is adopting a digital planning system using a task management app.","I implemented this change about six months ago to better organize my daily activities and commitments, especially during busy periods like exams and project deadlines."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62636","text":"A significant change that has helped me save a lot of time is adopting a digital planning system using a task management app. I implemented this change about six months ago to better organize my daily activities and commitments, especially during busy periods like exams and project deadlines. To implement this system, I began by inputting all my tasks, deadlines, and appointments into the app. I categorize my tasks into different sections, such as work, personal, and study, and I set reminders for important deadlines. This organization allows me to see everything at a glance, making it easier to prioritize what needs to be done each day. I also utilize features like recurring tasks and checklists, which streamline my workflow and keep me on track. Initially, I found it somewhat challenging to get used to the app, especially as I transitioned from paper-based planning. However, with regular use, I became more comfortable with it and started to appreciate its efficiency. Overall, I feel very positive about this change. It has significantly reduced the stress of forgetting important tasks and has made me more productive. The ability to quickly adjust my schedule and tasks on the go has been a game-changer. This digital planning system has not only saved me time but has also enhanced my overall organization, allowing me to focus on what truly matters in my daily life.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E8%8A%82%E7%BA%A6%E6%97%B6%E9%97%B4%E7%9A%84%E6%96%B9%E6%B3%95%2F%E6%94%B9%E5%8F%98&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8666&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-8692","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 送朋友的礼物","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8692,"passage":"<h2>送朋友的礼物</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-62797","sourceQuestionId":62797,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a gift you would like to buy for your friend\nYou should say:\nHow you knew your friend\nHow long you have known him/her\nHow you would choose a gift for him/her\nAnd explain why you would choose that gift for him/her"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["本题问想买给朋友的礼物，选一个未来计划，如书、相册或实用物品。先说明如何认识朋友及认识多久。","根据朋友的兴趣、需要与预算解释选礼物的过程，使用 would buy/would choose 等假设表达，不把未发生的送礼写成过去经历。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62797","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I’d like to talk about a gift I’d love to buy for my close friend, Iris.","I met Iris when I first moved to Beijing about a year ago."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62797","text":"I’d like to talk about a gift I’d love to buy for my close friend, Iris. I met Iris when I first moved to Beijing about a year ago. We were introduced through a mutual friend, and our bond quickly grew stronger due to our shared interests in travel, food, and meaningful conversations. Over the past year, we’ve become not only close friends but also great travel companions, with one of the highlights being our memorable trip to Jeju Island last winter. For Iris’s birthday, I would want to give her something that reflects her unique personality and interests. Iris is an avid reader and a big fan of self-improvement books, so I’d choose a beautifully bound edition of a book by one of her favorite authors. But I’d make it extra special by getting her a personalized bookplate with her name on it. Along with that, I would buy her a high-quality, leather-bound journal because she loves journaling her thoughts and ideas. I believe this would be the perfect gift because it’s something thoughtful and practical, showing that I know and appreciate her passions. Iris is always so considerate and supportive of everyone around her, so I want to give her something that encourages her creativity and personal growth. A gift like this not only aligns with her interests but also carries a personal touch, which I believe she would deeply appreciate.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E9%80%81%E6%9C%8B%E5%8F%8B%E7%9A%84%E7%A4%BC%E7%89%A9&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8692&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-9834","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 做困难的事情并成功的人","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9834,"passage":"<h2>做困难的事情并成功的人</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71171","sourceQuestionId":71171,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a person you know who did something difficult and was successful\nYou should say:\nWho this person is\nWhat difficult thing this person did\nWhy this person was successful\nAnd explain how you feel about this person"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选一个完成考试、学技能或克服困难的人。","按目标、困难、尝试与成功组织；突出你亲眼看到的努力，而不是只说他聪明。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71171","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I'd like to talk about my cousin, who overcame tremendous difficulties to become a successful AI researcher.","He grew up in a remote village with very limited educational resources."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71171","text":"I'd like to talk about my cousin, who overcame tremendous difficulties to become a successful AI researcher. He grew up in a remote village with very limited educational resources. His parents were farmers and couldn't afford any extra tutoring or learning materials. Despite this, he managed to teach himself using old textbooks and a second-hand computer. The most difficult thing he did was getting into Tsinghua University for his PhD. He failed the entrance exam twice, and many people around him told him to give up and find a stable job instead. But he didn't listen. He worked part-time jobs during the day, such as delivering food and tutoring, and studied late into the night. After three years of relentless effort, he finally passed the exam with the top score in his major. He is now a respected researcher at a leading tech company. He succeeded because of his extraordinary perseverance and self-learning ability. He never blamed his poor background; instead, he turned it into motivation. I deeply admire him. His story proves that a low starting point doesn't determine your destination. Whenever I face challenges, I think of him studying in a tiny rented room, and it gives me strength.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%81%9A%E5%9B%B0%E9%9A%BE%E7%9A%84%E4%BA%8B%E6%83%85%E5%B9%B6%E6%88%90%E5%8A%9F%E7%9A%84%E4%BA%BA&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9834&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-9835","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 改变重要决定","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9835,"passage":"<h2>改变重要决定</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71178","sourceQuestionId":71178,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a time when you changed an important decision of yours\nYou should say:\nWhen you changed the decision\nWhat the original decision was\nWhy you changed it\nAnd explain how you felt about the experience"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选曾改变的专业、旅行或购买决定。","说清原决定、触发改变的新信息、如何权衡，以及改变后的结果。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71178","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I changed an important decision during my second year of university.","Originally, I had decided to major in accounting because my parents said it was stable and would lead to a good job."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71178","text":"I changed an important decision during my second year of university. Originally, I had decided to major in accounting because my parents said it was stable and would lead to a good job. I followed their advice without thinking much. However, after taking some elective courses in digital media, I realized my true interest lay in creative work, not numbers. I struggled for weeks and finally changed my major to digital media. I felt both scared and liberated. Scared because I was going against my parents' expectations, but liberated because I was finally making a choice for myself. It turned out to be one of the best decisions I've ever made.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E6%94%B9%E5%8F%98%E9%87%8D%E8%A6%81%E5%86%B3%E5%AE%9A&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9835&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-9836","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 本地名人","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9836,"passage":"<h2>本地名人</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71180","sourceQuestionId":71180,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a famous person in your local area\nYou should say:\nWho this person is\nWhat he/she has done\nWhy he/she is popular\nAnd explain how you feel about this person"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选在当地有影响的人，如运动员、艺术家或社区工作者。","解释你如何知道他，并举一项具体贡献；区分本地知名与全国知名。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71180","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I'd like to talk about a famous person in my local area, Mr.","Wang."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71180","text":"I'd like to talk about a famous person in my local area, Mr. Wang. He is a retired teacher who has taught Chinese literature at our local high school for over thirty years. Many of his students went on to top universities. He is also a well-known calligrapher, and every Spring Festival he writes free couplets for the whole community. He is popular because he is kind, humble, and always willing to help. I deeply admire him. He represents the traditional values of knowledge and virtue. Seeing him makes me feel proud of my hometown.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E6%9C%AC%E5%9C%B0%E5%90%8D%E4%BA%BA&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9836&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-9837","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 对结果开心的重要决定","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9837,"passage":"<h2>对结果开心的重要决定</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71183","sourceQuestionId":71183,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a time you made an important decision and were happy with the result\nYou should say:\nWhat the decision was\nWhy you made the decision\nHow easy it was for you to make the decision\nAnd explain why you were happy with the result"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选一次让你满意的决定，如参加课程或接受机会。","比较当时两个选择，讲清选择依据和后来看到的结果，不只说结果很好。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71183","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I made an important decision last year to study abroad for my master's degree.","I was hesitant between finding a job immediately and continuing my education."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71183","text":"I made an important decision last year to study abroad for my master's degree. I was hesitant between finding a job immediately and continuing my education. I made this decision because I wanted to broaden my horizons and gain an international perspective, which would benefit my future career. It wasn't easy—I had to consider the high cost and being far from my parents. But I eventually received an offer from a good university and got a scholarship, which reduced the financial burden. I'm happy because the experience has already made me more independent and confident. It's a life-changing step.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%AF%B9%E7%BB%93%E6%9E%9C%E5%BC%80%E5%BF%83%E7%9A%84%E9%87%8D%E8%A6%81%E5%86%B3%E5%AE%9A&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9837&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-9838","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 快乐人士","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9838,"passage":"<h2>快乐人士</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71190","sourceQuestionId":71190,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a happy person you know\nYou should say:\nWho this person is\nWhat he/she is like\nHow he/she shows happiness\nAnd explain why you think he/she is a happy person"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选经常表现积极的一位熟人。","用一次他面对小挫折的反应展示快乐心态，再说明这怎样影响身边人。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71190","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I'd like to talk about my neighbour, Auntie Liu.","She is a retired kindergarten teacher in her sixties."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71190","text":"I'd like to talk about my neighbour, Auntie Liu. She is a retired kindergarten teacher in her sixties. She is always smiling and greets everyone warmly. She dances in the square every evening and often invites others to join. She also grows flowers on her balcony and gives some to neighbours. I think she is happy because she finds joy in small things and never complains. She told me once, 'Happiness is not about having a lot, but wanting what you have.' I admire her attitude and feel happier just being around her.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%BF%AB%E4%B9%90%E4%BA%BA%E5%A3%AB&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9838&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-9839","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 看过的名人采访","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9839,"passage":"<h2>看过的名人采访</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71194","sourceQuestionId":71194,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a time watched a famous person being interviewed\nYou should say:\nWho the famous person was\nWhat the interview was about\nWhen and where you watched the interview\nAnd explain how you felt about the interview"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选你看过且记得主题的采访。","交代人物、观看渠道与一个问题，说明哪句话或经历改变了你的看法。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71194","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I'd like to talk about an interview I watched with a famous entrepreneur, Lei Jun, the founder of Xiaomi.","I watched it on Bilibili last summer, around August."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71194","text":"I'd like to talk about an interview I watched with a famous entrepreneur, Lei Jun, the founder of Xiaomi. I watched it on Bilibili last summer, around August. The interview was about his journey of starting Xiaomi and the challenges of competing with global smartphone giants. He also talked about his philosophy of making technology affordable for everyone. I watched it at home on my phone at night. I felt very inspired. He was humble and practical. He said that success is not about being the smartest, but about persistence and caring for users. The interview changed my view of him from just a businessman to a true visionary. It motivated me to work harder on my own projects.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E7%9C%8B%E8%BF%87%E7%9A%84%E5%90%8D%E4%BA%BA%E9%87%87%E8%AE%BF&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9839&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-9840","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 和朋友度过的愉快夜晚","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9840,"passage":"<h2>和朋友度过的愉快夜晚</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71202","sourceQuestionId":71202,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe an enjoyable evening you had with your friends\nYou should say:\nWhen and where it was\nWhat you did\nWho you spent the evening with\nAnd explain why it was enjoyable"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选一次聚餐、散步或游戏夜。","用活动过程中的一个小插曲说明为什么开心，结尾联系友谊而非只描述食物。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71202","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I'd like to talk about a really enjoyable evening I spent with my best friends last summer.","It was a Friday evening in early July, at a riverside park near our university."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71202","text":"I'd like to talk about a really enjoyable evening I spent with my best friends last summer. It was a Friday evening in early July, at a riverside park near our university. We had all just finished our final exams, so we were finally free and relaxed. There were six of us, all close friends from the same department. We brought blankets, snacks, and a speaker. We sat on the grass by the river, listening to music and playing card games. As the sun set, the sky turned orange and pink, and the river reflected the colours beautifully. Later, we ordered some barbecue takeaway and chatted about our holiday plans. I remember laughing so hard at one friend's stories that my stomach hurt. We stayed until about eleven, just lying on the grass and looking at the stars. It was enjoyable because there was no pressure, no schedule. It was just pure friendship, good food, and a beautiful evening. The combination of nature, music, and close friends made it unforgettable.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%92%8C%E6%9C%8B%E5%8F%8B%E5%BA%A6%E8%BF%87%E7%9A%84%E6%84%89%E5%BF%AB%E5%A4%9C%E6%99%9A&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9840&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-9841","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 擅长做手工的人","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9841,"passage":"<h2>擅长做手工的人</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71204","sourceQuestionId":71204,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a person who is good at making things by hand\nYou should say:\nWho this person is\nWhat he/she makes\nWhy you think this person is good at making things by hand\nAnd explain how you feel about the person"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选会做陶艺、木工、编织或模型的人。","描述一种成品、制作过程的一步和需要的耐心，再说明你为何欣赏这项技能。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71204","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I'd like to talk about my grandfather, who is incredibly good at making things by hand.","He is a retired carpenter with hands as rough as tree bark."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71204","text":"I'd like to talk about my grandfather, who is incredibly good at making things by hand. He is a retired carpenter with hands as rough as tree bark. He makes all kinds of wooden things, including stools, bookshelves, and even intricate toy cars. He also weaves bamboo baskets and repairs broken furniture for neighbours. I think he is good at this because of decades of practice and genuine love for craftsmanship. He always says that machines can make things fast, but only hands can give things a soul. When he works, he is completely focused, and every joint he makes fits perfectly without any nails. I deeply admire him. In a world of mass production, his handmade pieces feel warm and alive. Watching him work is like watching an artist. Each object has its own character, and you can feel the patience and care behind it.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E6%93%85%E9%95%BF%E5%81%9A%E6%89%8B%E5%B7%A5%E7%9A%84%E4%BA%BA&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9841&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p2-9842","type":"speaking","title":"Part 2 · 听不感兴趣的话","book":"口语全集题目","part":2,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9842,"passage":"<h2>听不感兴趣的话</h2><p>Part 2</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71211","sourceQuestionId":71211,"type":"speaking","part":2,"text":"Describe a time when someone talked about something you were not interested in but you kept listening\nYou should say:\nWho the person was\nWhat he/she talked about\nWhy you kept listening\nAnd explain how you felt about the experience"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["选一次不得不听讲座、推销或长谈的经历。","说明内容为何与你无关、你如何保持礼貌，以及最后的感受或学到的沟通经验。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71211","approach":"用准备时间写关键词，覆盖题卡的每一项提示，按时间或因果顺序讲述。","example_direction":["I'd like to talk about a time when my uncle talked to me about his stamp collection for over an hour.","I have no interest in stamps at all, but I kept listening."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"用自己的经历替换人物和地点，脱稿练习连贯讲述。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71211","text":"I'd like to talk about a time when my uncle talked to me about his stamp collection for over an hour. I have no interest in stamps at all, but I kept listening. It happened last Spring Festival, after the family dinner. He was very excited, showing me albums of stamps from the 1980s. I kept listening because he is my elder and I respect him. Also, I could see how much this hobby meant to him. His eyes were shining while he talked. I didn't want to break his heart. I felt a bit bored but also warm inside. Seeing an older person so passionate about something was touching. I learned that sometimes listening is not about the content but about showing love and respect.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%90%AC%E4%B8%8D%E6%84%9F%E5%85%B4%E8%B6%A3%E7%9A%84%E8%AF%9D&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9842&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-8681","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 好的购物服务","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8681,"passage":"<h2>好的购物服务</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-62736","sourceQuestionId":62736,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Can consumption drive economic growth?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62737","sourceQuestionId":62737,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What are the advantages and disadvantages of shopping in small shops?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62738","sourceQuestionId":62738,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What are the advantages and disadvantages of shopping online?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62739","sourceQuestionId":62739,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What are the differences between online shopping and in-store shopping?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62740","sourceQuestionId":62740,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Why are shopping malls so popular in China?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62741","sourceQuestionId":62741,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Why do some people not like shopping in small shops?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62736","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Yes, absolutely.","Consumption is a primary driver of economic growth."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62737","approach":"先说明一项主要收益，再解释一项限制；分别说明机制，不只列词。","example_direction":["The main advantage of small shops is personalised, knowledgeable service and unique products you can't find in chain stores.","They often foster a sense of community."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62738","approach":"先说明一项主要收益，再解释一项限制；分别说明机制，不只列词。","example_direction":["The prime advantage of online shopping is unparalleled convenience and choice, available 24/7 from anywhere.","Key disadvantages include the inability to inspect items beforehand, delivery delays, the risk of receiving faulty goods, and the environmental impact of packaging and shipping."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62739","approach":"按同一标准比较两方，例如成本、便利或态度，并举对照例子。","example_direction":["The core difference lies in the experience.","In-store shopping allows you to see, touch, and try products immediately, and offers personal service."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62740","approach":"解释一至两个原因，用因果链说明行为如何产生，再承认人群差异。","example_direction":["Shopping malls are immensely popular in China because they are more than just retail spaces; they are comprehensive lifestyle hubs.","They offer climate-controlled comfort, a wide variety of brands and restaurants under one roof, and serve as social venues where families and friends spend entire weekends shopping, dining, and watching movies."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62741","approach":"解释一至两个原因，用因果链说明行为如何产生，再承认人群差异。","example_direction":["Some people avoid small shops due to perceptions of higher prices, less variety, and inconsistent quality.","Others may find the service overly attentive or feel pressure to buy."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62736","text":"Yes, absolutely. Consumption is a primary driver of economic growth. When consumers spend money on goods and services, it increases demand, which encourages businesses to produce more. This cycle leads to higher revenues for companies, job creation, increased investments, and greater tax revenues for the government, all of which stimulate the broader economy.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62737","text":"The main advantage of small shops is personalised, knowledgeable service and unique products you can't find in chain stores. They often foster a sense of community. The disadvantages can include higher prices due to lower economies of scale, limited selection, and sometimes less convenient operating hours.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62738","text":"The prime advantage of online shopping is unparalleled convenience and choice, available 24/7 from anywhere. Key disadvantages include the inability to inspect items beforehand, delivery delays, the risk of receiving faulty goods, and the environmental impact of packaging and shipping.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62739","text":"The core difference lies in the experience. In-store shopping allows you to see, touch, and try products immediately, and offers personal service. Online shopping provides superior convenience, a vastly larger selection, and the ability to easily compare prices, but you must wait for delivery and deal with the hassle of returns.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62740","text":"Shopping malls are immensely popular in China because they are more than just retail spaces; they are comprehensive lifestyle hubs. They offer climate-controlled comfort, a wide variety of brands and restaurants under one roof, and serve as social venues where families and friends spend entire weekends shopping, dining, and watching movies.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62741","text":"Some people avoid small shops due to perceptions of higher prices, less variety, and inconsistent quality. Others may find the service overly attentive or feel pressure to buy. The convenience of one-stop shopping in large malls or online also draws people away from smaller, specialised stores.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%A5%BD%E7%9A%84%E8%B4%AD%E7%89%A9%E6%9C%8D%E5%8A%A1&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8681&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-8702","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 钦佩的运动员","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8702,"passage":"<h2>钦佩的运动员</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-62862","sourceQuestionId":62862,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Is it easy to identify children's talents?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62863","sourceQuestionId":62863,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Is talent important in sports?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62864","sourceQuestionId":62864,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Should students have physical education and do sports at school?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62865","sourceQuestionId":62865,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What is the most popular sport in your country?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62866","sourceQuestionId":62866,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What qualities should an athlete have?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62867","sourceQuestionId":62867,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Why are there so few top athletes?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62862","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Identifying children's talents can be challenging because interests and abilities develop over time.","While some children show early aptitude, others may bloom later."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62863","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Talent is undoubtedly important in sports as it provides a natural advantage, such as superior coordination, speed, or strength.","However, talent alone is insufficient; hard work, proper training, and mental toughness are often what differentiate a good athlete from a great one."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62864","approach":"明确主张，再解释理由和可能代价；必要时提出实施条件。","example_direction":["Physical education and sports are absolutely essential in schools.","They not only promote physical health and combat childhood obesity but also teach crucial life skills such as teamwork, discipline, and resilience."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62865","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["The most popular sport in China is undoubtedly basketball, driven by the NBA's influence and domestic leagues.","Football also has a massive following, along with traditional sports like badminton and table tennis, which are widely played at recreational and competitive levels."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62866","approach":"明确主张，再解释理由和可能代价；必要时提出实施条件。","example_direction":["An athlete should possess a combination of physical prowess and mental strength.","Key qualities include discipline, dedication, resilience, and the ability to perform under pressure."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62867","approach":"解释一至两个原因，用因果链说明行为如何产生，再承认人群差异。","example_direction":["There are few top athletes because reaching the elite level requires a rare combination of innate talent, relentless training, access to resources, and mental fortitude.","Many drop out due to injuries, burnout, or lack of support, making the path to the top extremely narrow and highly competitive."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62862","text":"Identifying children's talents can be challenging because interests and abilities develop over time. While some children show early aptitude, others may bloom later. Observation, exposure to diverse activities, and encouragement are key, but pressure should be avoided to allow organic growth.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62863","text":"Talent is undoubtedly important in sports as it provides a natural advantage, such as superior coordination, speed, or strength. However, talent alone is insufficient; hard work, proper training, and mental toughness are often what differentiate a good athlete from a great one.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62864","text":"Physical education and sports are absolutely essential in schools. They not only promote physical health and combat childhood obesity but also teach crucial life skills such as teamwork, discipline, and resilience. Engaging in sports can reduce stress, improve concentration, and foster a sense of community among students.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62865","text":"The most popular sport in China is undoubtedly basketball, driven by the NBA's influence and domestic leagues. Football also has a massive following, along with traditional sports like badminton and table tennis, which are widely played at recreational and competitive levels.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62866","text":"An athlete should possess a combination of physical prowess and mental strength. Key qualities include discipline, dedication, resilience, and the ability to perform under pressure. Team players also need strong communication and cooperation skills, while individual athletes must have intense focus and self-motivation.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62867","text":"There are few top athletes because reaching the elite level requires a rare combination of innate talent, relentless training, access to resources, and mental fortitude. Many drop out due to injuries, burnout, or lack of support, making the path to the top extremely narrow and highly competitive.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E9%92%A6%E4%BD%A9%E7%9A%84%E8%BF%90%E5%8A%A8%E5%91%98&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8702&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-8503","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 嘈杂地","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8503,"passage":"<h2>嘈杂地</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-61562","sourceQuestionId":61562,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Do you think it is good for children to make noise?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61563","sourceQuestionId":61563,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"How can people consider others' feelings when chatting in public?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61564","sourceQuestionId":61564,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"How would people usually respond to noises in your country?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61565","sourceQuestionId":61565,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Should children not be allowed to make noise under any circumstances?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61566","sourceQuestionId":61566,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What kinds of noises are there in our life?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61567","sourceQuestionId":61567,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Which area is exposed to noise more, the city or the countryside?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61562","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Moderate noise is natural and healthy for children's expression and development.","Playful noise often indicates creativity, social interaction and physical activity."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61563","approach":"说明具体方式、负责主体和作用机制，再举一种情境。","example_direction":["Keeping voices at moderate levels shows consideration.","Avoiding sensitive topics that might discomfort nearby listeners is polite."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61564","approach":"说明具体方式、负责主体和作用机制，再举一种情境。","example_direction":["Responses vary by noise type and cultural norms.","Construction noise during daytime is generally tolerated, while late-night disturbances often prompt complaints."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61565","approach":"明确主张，再解释理由和可能代价；必要时提出实施条件。","example_direction":["Absolute silence expectations are unrealistic and potentially harmful to children's emotional and social development.","However, reasonable boundaries should exist - libraries versus playgrounds have different norms."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61566","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Well, in our daily lives, we encounter a wide variety of noises, some pleasant and others quite disruptive.","For instance, urban areas are often filled with traffic sounds—car horns, engine noises, and the rumbling of buses or trains."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61567","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Cities undoubtedly have more constant and varied noise pollution - traffic, construction, crowds, and industry create relentless background noise.","Rural areas experience quieter environments overall, though they have distinctive noises like farm equipment or wildlife."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61562","text":"Moderate noise is natural and healthy for children's expression and development. Playful noise often indicates creativity, social interaction and physical activity. However, context matters - learning quiet focus is equally important. The key is teaching appropriate times and places for louder play, not suppressing natural exuberance completely. Balance fosters both self-expression and consideration for others.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61563","text":"Keeping voices at moderate levels shows consideration. Avoiding sensitive topics that might discomfort nearby listeners is polite. Reading the environment - quieter tones in confined spaces like elevators - demonstrates awareness. Pausing conversations when passing closely by others respects personal space. Essentially, maintaining spatial and volume awareness while balancing one's right to converse with others' right to peace.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61564","text":"Responses vary by noise type and cultural norms. Construction noise during daytime is generally tolerated, while late-night disturbances often prompt complaints. Neighbors might politely request volume reduction for persistent issues. In public transport, loud conversations are sometimes frowned upon. Overall, there's growing awareness of noise pollution's health impacts, leading to more regulations and personal noise-cancelling solutions like headphones.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61565","text":"Absolute silence expectations are unrealistic and potentially harmful to children's emotional and social development. However, reasonable boundaries should exist - libraries versus playgrounds have different norms. Teaching noise appropriateness helps children navigate social expectations. The goal should be helping children understand context rather than enforcing complete silence, which could inhibit their confidence and natural expressiveness.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61566","text":"Well, in our daily lives, we encounter a wide variety of noises, some pleasant and others quite disruptive. For instance, urban areas are often filled with traffic sounds—car horns, engine noises, and the rumbling of buses or trains. Then there are human-made noises like conversations, laughter, or even loud arguments, which are common in public spaces.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61567","text":"Cities undoubtedly have more constant and varied noise pollution - traffic, construction, crowds, and industry create relentless background noise. Rural areas experience quieter environments overall, though they have distinctive noises like farm equipment or wildlife. However, countryside noises are often less intrusive and more rhythmic than urban soundscapes. The city's density and activity levels guarantee greater noise exposure at all hours.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%98%88%E6%9D%82%E5%9C%B0&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8503&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-8559","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 想再去一次的城市","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8559,"passage":"<h2>想再去一次的城市</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-61929","sourceQuestionId":61929,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Do you think it is possible that all of the population move to cities?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61930","sourceQuestionId":61930,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Do you think people in the countryside are friendlier than people in the city?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61931","sourceQuestionId":61931,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Some people say large cities are suitable for old people. What do you think?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61932","sourceQuestionId":61932,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What should the government do to improve citizens' safety?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61933","sourceQuestionId":61933,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What's the difference between the city and the countryside?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61927","sourceQuestionId":61927,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Are there any changes in your city?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61929","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["A complete urban migration is neither feasible nor sustainable.","While cities offer economic opportunities, rural areas remain vital for agriculture, ecological balance, and cultural preservation."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61930","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Rural communities often exhibit closer-knit social bonds due to smaller populations and shared traditions—like village festivals or cooperative farming.","However, city dwellers aren't inherently less friendly; urban anonymity stems from population density and fast-paced lifestyles."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61931","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["While cities provide critical advantages like accessible healthcare and senior-friendly infrastructure (elevated walkways, 24/7 pharmacies), they also pose challenges.","Noise pollution and fast-paced environments may stress elderly residents, whereas rural areas offer tranquility."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61932","approach":"明确主张，再解释理由和可能代价；必要时提出实施条件。","example_direction":["Enhance surveillance in high-risk areas using AI cameras while ensuring privacy safeguards.","Improve street lighting and pedestrian pathways to deter crime."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61933","approach":"按同一标准比较两方，例如成本、便利或态度，并举对照例子。","example_direction":["Cities and rural areas differ starkly in pace, infrastructure, and lifestyle.","Urban centers offer high-density living with advanced amenities—metro systems, hospitals, and cultural hubs—but grapple with pollution and stress."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61927","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Hangzhou has embraced smart-city initiatives: AI-driven traffic management reduces congestion, while eco-parks like Xixi Wetland combat urban heat.","The tech boom, centered around Alibaba, has attracted global talent, diversifying the population."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61929","text":"A complete urban migration is neither feasible nor sustainable. While cities offer economic opportunities, rural areas remain vital for agriculture, ecological balance, and cultural preservation. Overcrowding would strain infrastructure (e.g., Mumbai's slums) and exacerbate housing crises. Additionally, many industries like farming or renewable energy projects require rural spaces. Governments should instead focus on balanced development—improving rural healthcare and digital connectivity to reduce urban-rural disparities while maintaining demographic diversity for long-term societal resilience.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61930","text":"Rural communities often exhibit closer-knit social bonds due to smaller populations and shared traditions—like village festivals or cooperative farming. However, city dwellers aren't inherently less friendly; urban anonymity stems from population density and fast-paced lifestyles. Studies (e.g., Social Psychology Quarterly) note that rural residents greet strangers more, while cities foster niche friendships (e.g., coworking spaces). Context matters: a Tokyo commuter may seem aloof but could be deeply engaged in neighborhood volunteer groups. Cultural norms, not geography alone, shape behavior.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61931","text":"While cities provide critical advantages like accessible healthcare and senior-friendly infrastructure (elevated walkways, 24/7 pharmacies), they also pose challenges. Noise pollution and fast-paced environments may stress elderly residents, whereas rural areas offer tranquility. However, urban community programs (e.g., Tokyo's dementia-friendly districts) and proximity to family support can offset these issues. Ultimately, suitability depends on individual needs—mobility-impaired seniors benefit from cities' amenities, but those prioritizing affordability and quiet might prefer villages with tailored services.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61932","text":"Enhance surveillance in high-risk areas using AI cameras while ensuring privacy safeguards. Improve street lighting and pedestrian pathways to deter crime. Public campaigns on cyber safety and scam awareness are vital as digital threats rise. Strengthen community policing for faster emergency response and foster neighborhood watch programs. Finally, addressing mental health through accessible counseling can reduce social instability at its root.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61933","text":"Cities and rural areas differ starkly in pace, infrastructure, and lifestyle. Urban centers offer high-density living with advanced amenities—metro systems, hospitals, and cultural hubs—but grapple with pollution and stress. Conversely, villages prioritize community bonds and natural landscapes, though limited healthcare or transport persists. Economically, cities thrive on industries like finance, while agriculture dominates rural livelihoods. Environmentally, countryside air and biodiversity surpass cities' concrete sprawl. These contrasts reflect trade-offs between convenience and tranquility, each appealing to different life stages or priorities.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61927","text":"Hangzhou has embraced smart-city initiatives: AI-driven traffic management reduces congestion, while eco-parks like Xixi Wetland combat urban heat. The tech boom, centered around Alibaba, has attracted global talent, diversifying the population. However, rapid urbanization strains infrastructure, prompting investments in metro expansions and affordable housing. Cultural preservation efforts, like restoring ancient tea villages, balance modernity with heritage.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E6%83%B3%E5%86%8D%E5%8E%BB%E4%B8%80%E6%AC%A1%E7%9A%84%E5%9F%8E%E5%B8%82&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8559&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-8417","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 一见且想再见的人","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8417,"passage":"<h2>一见且想再见的人</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-60985","sourceQuestionId":60985,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"How do people make friends in China?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60986","sourceQuestionId":60986,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Is it important to have the same hobbies and interests when making friends?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60987","sourceQuestionId":60987,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"On what occasions do people like to make friends?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60988","sourceQuestionId":60988,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What can we do to leave a good impression on people we meet for the first time?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60989","sourceQuestionId":60989,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What qualities make true friends?"},{"id":"igopx-question-60990","sourceQuestionId":60990,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What should we not talk about when we meet a person for the first time?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60985","approach":"说明具体方式、负责主体和作用机制，再举一种情境。","example_direction":["In China, people typically make friends through shared experiences, such as school, work, or mutual interests.","For example, students often form friendships through group projects or extracurricular activities, while colleagues bond over work-related tasks or after-hours socializing."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60986","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["While having shared hobbies and interests can certainly make it easier to form connections, it’s not essential for a true friendship.","Common interests provide a foundation for conversation and shared activities, which can strengthen bonds."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60987","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["People tend to make friends on occasions where they can engage in social activities or share experiences.","Common occasions include starting a new job or school, where people are naturally inclined to meet others in similar situations."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60988","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["To leave a good impression, it's important to be genuine, polite, and attentive.","Making eye contact and offering a firm handshake can convey confidence and friendliness."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60989","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["True friends are characterized by qualities like trust, loyalty, empathy, and honesty.","Trust is essential because friends need to feel comfortable confiding in each other without fear of betrayal."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60990","approach":"明确主张，再解释理由和可能代价；必要时提出实施条件。","example_direction":["When meeting someone for the first time, it's important to avoid topics that might be too personal or controversial, such as politics, religion, or personal finances.","These topics can make people uncomfortable or spark heated debates."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-60985","text":"In China, people typically make friends through shared experiences, such as school, work, or mutual interests. For example, students often form friendships through group projects or extracurricular activities, while colleagues bond over work-related tasks or after-hours socializing. Social networks, both online and offline, play a significant role, with platforms like WeChat and QQ allowing people to connect easily. Additionally, family and close friends often introduce individuals to new people, expanding their social circles. Overall, making friends in China is often centered around networking, shared activities, and mutual connections, rather than random encounters.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60986","text":"While having shared hobbies and interests can certainly make it easier to form connections, it’s not essential for a true friendship. Common interests provide a foundation for conversation and shared activities, which can strengthen bonds. However, some of the most rewarding friendships are built on differences, where individuals learn from each other’s perspectives and broaden their horizons. Ultimately, qualities like trust, respect, and emotional support are far more important for a lasting friendship. People may enjoy diverse hobbies, but the depth of understanding and shared values often matter more than mutual interests.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60987","text":"People tend to make friends on occasions where they can engage in social activities or share experiences. Common occasions include starting a new job or school, where people are naturally inclined to meet others in similar situations. Social events like parties, festivals, or weddings are also opportunities for people to connect, as they provide a relaxed atmosphere for conversations. Additionally, shared hobbies, such as joining a sports team or a community group, create natural opportunities to form friendships based on common interests. In essence, people make friends during events that foster interaction and shared experiences.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60988","text":"To leave a good impression, it's important to be genuine, polite, and attentive. Making eye contact and offering a firm handshake can convey confidence and friendliness. Listening actively and showing interest in the other person’s words helps build rapport. Additionally, a positive attitude and good manners go a long way. Dressing appropriately for the occasion and being punctual also demonstrate respect for the other person’s time and presence, which can create a lasting positive impact.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60989","text":"True friends are characterized by qualities like trust, loyalty, empathy, and honesty. Trust is essential because friends need to feel comfortable confiding in each other without fear of betrayal. Loyalty means standing by each other through both good and challenging times. Empathy allows friends to understand and support each other emotionally, while honesty fosters clear communication and avoids misunderstandings. Additionally, mutual respect and a sense of humor can strengthen the bond, as these qualities help friends navigate differences and enjoy each other’s company over time. Ultimately, it’s a combination of emotional support and shared values that defines true friendship.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-60990","text":"When meeting someone for the first time, it's important to avoid topics that might be too personal or controversial, such as politics, religion, or personal finances. These topics can make people uncomfortable or spark heated debates. Similarly, asking overly personal questions about someone’s relationships or health is inappropriate. Instead, it’s best to focus on neutral subjects, such as hobbies, travel experiences, or shared interests, which create a positive, relaxed atmosphere and allow the conversation to flow naturally.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E4%B8%80%E8%A7%81%E4%B8%94%E6%83%B3%E5%86%8D%E8%A7%81%E7%9A%84%E4%BA%BA&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8417&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-8466","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 印象深刻的课程","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8466,"passage":"<h2>印象深刻的课程</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-61324","sourceQuestionId":61324,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Can technology help people remember things better? How?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61325","sourceQuestionId":61325,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Do people like things of memorial significance?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61326","sourceQuestionId":61326,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What can we learn from history?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61327","sourceQuestionId":61327,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What do people need to remember in their daily lives?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61328","sourceQuestionId":61328,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Which can help people remember things better, words or photos?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61329","sourceQuestionId":61329,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Why do some people have a better memory than others?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61324","approach":"说明具体方式、负责主体和作用机制，再举一种情境。","example_direction":["Yes, technology can significantly enhance memory retention.","Digital tools like note-taking apps, reminders, and calendar alerts help people organize information and set reminders, ensuring important tasks are not forgotten."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61325","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Yes, many people are drawn to items of memorial significance because they evoke cherished memories and serve as a connection to the past.","For instance, personal mementos like photographs, gifts, or heirlooms often remind people of special moments or loved ones, creating a sense of continuity in their lives."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61326","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["History offers valuable lessons by helping us understand the successes and failures of past civilizations.","It teaches us about human behavior, the consequences of political decisions, and the importance of social and cultural progress."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61327","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["In daily life, people need to remember a range of practical and personal responsibilities.","This includes managing time effectively, such as meeting work deadlines or attending appointments."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61328","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Both words and photos can aid memory, but they serve different purposes.","Words are effective for recalling detailed information and abstract concepts."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61329","approach":"解释一至两个原因，用因果链说明行为如何产生，再承认人群差异。","example_direction":["Some people have a better memory than others due to a combination of genetic factors, brain structure, and lifestyle habits.","Research suggests that certain genetic traits can influence how efficiently the brain processes and stores information."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61324","text":"Yes, technology can significantly enhance memory retention. Digital tools like note-taking apps, reminders, and calendar alerts help people organize information and set reminders, ensuring important tasks are not forgotten. Additionally, apps that use spaced repetition techniques can optimize learning by reinforcing information at strategic intervals. Virtual reality (VR) and augmented reality (AR) can also improve memory by creating immersive experiences that engage multiple senses, making the information more memorable. Moreover, cloud storage allows easy access to photos, documents, and other materials, helping people recall details from the past by simply revisiting digital archives.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61325","text":"Yes, many people are drawn to items of memorial significance because they evoke cherished memories and serve as a connection to the past. For instance, personal mementos like photographs, gifts, or heirlooms often remind people of special moments or loved ones, creating a sense of continuity in their lives. Moreover, historical landmarks or objects, such as monuments or cultural artifacts, help preserve a collective history, instilling a sense of identity and pride. These items allow individuals to reflect on their experiences and heritage, fostering emotional connections that transcend time.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61326","text":"History offers valuable lessons by helping us understand the successes and failures of past civilizations. It teaches us about human behavior, the consequences of political decisions, and the importance of social and cultural progress. By studying history, we can identify patterns, learn from mistakes, and avoid repeating them. It also provides insight into how innovations, conflicts, and cultural exchanges have shaped the world we live in today, offering guidance for making informed decisions for the future.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61327","text":"In daily life, people need to remember a range of practical and personal responsibilities. This includes managing time effectively, such as meeting work deadlines or attending appointments. Health is another key consideration, so remembering to eat well, exercise, and get enough rest is vital. People should also remember to stay connected with family and friends to maintain social relationships. Additionally, being mindful of environmental impacts and practicing sustainable habits is becoming increasingly important for long-term well-being.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61328","text":"Both words and photos can aid memory, but they serve different purposes. Words are effective for recalling detailed information and abstract concepts. They help organize thoughts and create a narrative that makes facts easier to remember. On the other hand, photos have a powerful visual impact, evoking emotions and offering a quick, vivid recollection of specific moments. Studies suggest that images can enhance memory retention by triggering sensory details that words alone may not convey. Ultimately, combining both—such as with captions or stories accompanying photos—can be the most effective way to improve memory and recall.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61329","text":"Some people have a better memory than others due to a combination of genetic factors, brain structure, and lifestyle habits. Research suggests that certain genetic traits can influence how efficiently the brain processes and stores information. Additionally, individuals who engage in activities that stimulate the brain, such as reading, learning new skills, or exercising regularly, tend to have better cognitive function. Furthermore, a healthy lifestyle—adequate sleep, good nutrition, and stress management—also plays a significant role in improving memory. Ultimately, both biology and habits contribute to the differences in memory between individuals.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%8D%B0%E8%B1%A1%E6%B7%B1%E5%88%BB%E7%9A%84%E8%AF%BE%E7%A8%8B&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8466&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-8538","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 帮助他人","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8538,"passage":"<h2>帮助他人</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-61787","sourceQuestionId":61787,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Can kids provide any help to parents?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61788","sourceQuestionId":61788,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Should children be taught to be kind to others?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61789","sourceQuestionId":61789,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Should parents give children advice? Why?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61790","sourceQuestionId":61790,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Should parents help their kids with their homework?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61791","sourceQuestionId":61791,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Should people be very kind when they help others?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61792","sourceQuestionId":61792,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What kind of advice should parents give to their children?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61787","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Certainly, children can provide help and support to their parents, strengthening family bonds and teaching valuable life skills.","Firstly, kids can assist with household chores, such as cleaning, setting the table, or caring for pets."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61788","approach":"明确主张，再解释理由和可能代价；必要时提出实施条件。","example_direction":["Teaching children to be kind to others is essential for their social and moral development.","It helps them build crucial social skills like empathy and effective communication, fosters conflict resolution abilities, and reduces the likelihood of bullying."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61789","approach":"解释一至两个原因，用因果链说明行为如何产生，再承认人群差异。","example_direction":["Yes, parents should give children advice because it serves several crucial purposes.","Firstly, children lack the life experience and knowledge to make informed decisions, so parental guidance is essential for their well-being and development."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61790","approach":"明确主张，再解释理由和可能代价；必要时提出实施条件。","example_direction":["Parents should consider several factors when deciding whether to help their kids with homework.","Offering guidance and support can be beneficial, especially for younger children or when tasks are particularly challenging."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61791","approach":"明确主张，再解释理由和可能代价；必要时提出实施条件。","example_direction":["Yes, kindness is a fundamental quality when offering help to others.","It embodies empathy, compassion, and a genuine desire to alleviate someone's burdens or difficulties."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61792","approach":"明确主张，再解释理由和可能代价；必要时提出实施条件。","example_direction":["Parents can provide invaluable advice to their children in various areas of life.","They should encourage a love of learning, emphasizing the importance of education and personal growth."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61787","text":"Certainly, children can provide help and support to their parents, strengthening family bonds and teaching valuable life skills. Firstly, kids can assist with household chores, such as cleaning, setting the table, or caring for pets. These responsibilities not only lighten the load for parents but also teach children about responsibility and teamwork.\nSecondly, children can share their educational experiences and knowledge, keeping parents informed about what they're learning at school. They can also provide tech-savvy assistance, helping parents navigate technology and digital platforms.\nEmotionally, kids can offer companionship, understanding, and comfort to their parents, fostering strong emotional connections within the family.\nMoreover, children's creativity and entertainment talents, such as artwork, music, or storytelling, can bring joy and fun to family life.\nLastly, children can learn valuable life lessons from their parents, benefiting from their experiences and wisdom.\nOverall, children can play a meaningful role in supporting their parents while also gaining important life skills and contributing to a harmonious family environment.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61788","text":"Teaching children to be kind to others is essential for their social and moral development. It helps them build crucial social skills like empathy and effective communication, fosters conflict resolution abilities, and reduces the likelihood of bullying. Kindness also contributes to a child's emotional well-being, boosting self-esteem and mental health.\nBy learning kindness, children develop empathy and compassion, which are vital for forming positive relationships and contributing positively to their communities. Moreover, instilling kindness in children often results in the development of lifelong values that promote a more compassionate and caring society.\nIncorporating kindness into educational curricula and parenting practices not only benefits individual children but also contributes to a more harmonious and empathetic society overall.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61789","text":"Yes, parents should give children advice because it serves several crucial purposes. Firstly, children lack the life experience and knowledge to make informed decisions, so parental guidance is essential for their well-being and development. Parents can offer advice on safety, values, and ethics to protect their children and instill important principles.\nAdvice also plays a role in skill development, helping children acquire problem-solving, decision-making, and conflict resolution skills. It serves as a form of mentorship, where parents share their wisdom and experiences, providing valuable insights.\nFurthermore, advice offers emotional support, helping children cope with stress and difficult emotions. As children grow, the advice they receive prepares them for greater independence and self-reliance in adulthood.\nHowever, it's vital to strike a balance between offering guidance and allowing children to learn from their experiences. Effective communication and open dialogue are essential for successful advice-giving, fostering a healthy parent-child relationship.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61790","text":"Parents should consider several factors when deciding whether to help their kids with homework. Offering guidance and support can be beneficial, especially for younger children or when tasks are particularly challenging. It can also provide valuable bonding opportunities and reduce stress.\nHowever, it's important to strike a balance. Overly assisting children can hinder their independence and problem-solving skills. Allowing children to complete homework independently fosters critical thinking and time management skills. It also ensures that they take responsibility for their education.\nParents should gauge their child's needs and gradually encourage more independence as the child grows. Ensuring equality in educational support is crucial, as not all children have access to parental assistance. Ultimately, the goal should be to empower children to become self-reliant learners while providing appropriate guidance when necessary.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61791","text":"Yes, kindness is a fundamental quality when offering help to others. It embodies empathy, compassion, and a genuine desire to alleviate someone's burdens or difficulties. Kindness not only addresses immediate needs but also promotes positive emotional connections. It fosters trust, dignity, and respect, ensuring that those receiving help are treated with empathy and consideration.\nMoreover, kindness has a far-reaching impact, generating feelings of fulfillment and happiness for both the giver and receiver. It encourages cooperation and collaboration, often leading to more effective and sustainable solutions to problems. Acts of kindness can build a sense of community and unity, inspiring others to engage in similar benevolent actions.\nIn times of adversity, the kindness of others provides emotional healing and comfort, helping individuals navigate challenges. While kindness is vital, it's essential to be sensitive to individual needs and boundaries, ensuring that the help offered is both well-intentioned and genuinely beneficial. Ultimately, kindness is the cornerstone of meaningful and effective assistance to others.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61792","text":"Parents can provide invaluable advice to their children in various areas of life. They should encourage a love of learning, emphasizing the importance of education and personal growth. Teaching strong values, ethics, and kindness is essential to fostering empathy and respect for others.\nIndependence and responsibility are critical life skills, teaching children to make decisions and learn from their experiences. Resilience should be encouraged, helping them see challenges as opportunities for growth.\nEffective communication skills are vital for building healthy relationships, whether with friends, family, or romantic partners. Parents should also promote physical and mental well-being, stressing the importance of a balanced lifestyle and seeking help when needed.\nFinancial literacy and responsible money management are essential life skills. Goal setting and planning help children work towards their aspirations, and critical thinking fosters problem-solving abilities.\nParents should teach safety awareness and online safety. Promoting respect for diversity and embracing different perspectives is crucial. Most importantly, unconditional love and acceptance form the foundation for a child's self-esteem and self-acceptance.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%B8%AE%E5%8A%A9%E4%BB%96%E4%BA%BA&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8538&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-8583","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 拥挤地方","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8583,"passage":"<h2>拥挤地方</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-62089","sourceQuestionId":62089,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Do you think it is a good trend to have more big cities?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62090","sourceQuestionId":62090,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Do you think there are some people who enjoy crowded places?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62091","sourceQuestionId":62091,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Which cities are crowded in your country?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62092","sourceQuestionId":62092,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Why do people go to crowded places?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62093","sourceQuestionId":62093,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Will people use bikes more or less in cities in the future?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62094","sourceQuestionId":62094,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Will there be more or less green space in cities in the future?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62089","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["The trend toward more big cities can be both beneficial and challenging.","On one hand, large cities often drive economic growth, innovation, and cultural exchange, offering diverse opportunities and amenities."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62090","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Yes, some people genuinely enjoy crowded places.","They often find the energy and vibrancy of such environments stimulating and exciting."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62091","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["In my country, some of the most crowded cities include Beijing, Shanghai, and Guangzhou.","These cities are major economic and cultural centers, attracting millions of people for work, education, and better living opportunities."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62092","approach":"解释一至两个原因，用因果链说明行为如何产生，再承认人群差异。","example_direction":["People often go to crowded places for several reasons.","Social interaction is a major factor; bustling environments like markets, concerts, or festivals offer opportunities to connect with others and enjoy communal experiences."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62093","approach":"区分预测与事实，说明变化驱动因素，并保留条件或不确定性。","example_direction":["People are likely to use bikes more in cities in the future as awareness of environmental issues, health benefits, and the need to reduce traffic congestion grows.","Many cities are investing in better cycling infrastructure, such as dedicated bike lanes and bike-sharing programs, to make biking safer and more convenient."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62094","approach":"区分预测与事实，说明变化驱动因素，并保留条件或不确定性。","example_direction":["In the future, it’s likely that cities will have more green spaces as urban planning increasingly prioritizes sustainability and quality of life.","Many cities are recognizing the benefits of parks, green roofs, and urban gardens in improving air quality, reducing heat, and providing residents with recreational areas."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62089","text":"The trend toward more big cities can be both beneficial and challenging. On one hand, large cities often drive economic growth, innovation, and cultural exchange, offering diverse opportunities and amenities. They can also foster greater efficiency in services and infrastructure. However, rapid urbanization can strain resources, lead to overcrowding, and exacerbate issues like pollution and inequality. Balancing growth with sustainable planning and investment in infrastructure is crucial. Ideally, urban expansion should be managed thoughtfully to ensure that the benefits of big cities are maximized while mitigating potential downsides.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62090","text":"Yes, some people genuinely enjoy crowded places. They often find the energy and vibrancy of such environments stimulating and exciting. For instance, events like music festivals, sports games, and bustling markets offer a lively atmosphere and a sense of shared experience that many find invigorating. These crowded settings can provide opportunities for social interaction, cultural immersion, and entertainment, making them appealing to those who thrive in dynamic and active environments. While crowded places might be overwhelming for some, others relish the excitement and social opportunities they present.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62091","text":"In my country, some of the most crowded cities include Beijing, Shanghai, and Guangzhou. These cities are major economic and cultural centers, attracting millions of people for work, education, and better living opportunities. Beijing, the capital, is known for its government institutions, historical landmarks, and dense population. Shanghai is a global financial hub with a dynamic lifestyle and one of the busiest ports in the world, making it highly populated. Guangzhou, in the south, is a key commercial city with a rich history and a vibrant trade scene. Other crowded cities include Shenzhen, known for its tech industry, and Chongqing, which has a rapidly growing population due to its economic expansion.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62092","text":"People often go to crowded places for several reasons. Social interaction is a major factor; bustling environments like markets, concerts, or festivals offer opportunities to connect with others and enjoy communal experiences. Additionally, crowded places frequently feature popular attractions or events, drawing individuals who seek entertainment or unique experiences. For many, the vibrant atmosphere and the sense of being part of something larger can be invigorating. Despite the potential for discomfort, the energy and opportunities provided by crowded places can be a strong pull for many people.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62093","text":"People are likely to use bikes more in cities in the future as awareness of environmental issues, health benefits, and the need to reduce traffic congestion grows. Many cities are investing in better cycling infrastructure, such as dedicated bike lanes and bike-sharing programs, to make biking safer and more convenient. Advancements in electric bikes also make cycling accessible to a broader range of people, including those who need to travel longer distances or navigate challenging terrains. Additionally, as urban areas continue to prioritize sustainable transport options, biking is expected to become an increasingly popular choice. Overall, the trend suggests a rise in cycling as cities work towards creating more eco-friendly and efficient transportation systems.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62094","text":"In the future, it’s likely that cities will have more green spaces as urban planning increasingly prioritizes sustainability and quality of life. Many cities are recognizing the benefits of parks, green roofs, and urban gardens in improving air quality, reducing heat, and providing residents with recreational areas. There is a growing trend towards integrating nature into urban environments, driven by the need to combat climate change and enhance public health. However, the extent of green space development will vary depending on each city’s resources, policies, and commitment to environmental initiatives. While some cities may struggle with space constraints, the overall direction points towards more green, livable urban landscapes.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E6%8B%A5%E6%8C%A4%E5%9C%B0%E6%96%B9&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8583&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-8476","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 受欢迎的人","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8476,"passage":"<h2>受欢迎的人</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-61386","sourceQuestionId":61386,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Do you think good teachers are always popular among students?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61387","sourceQuestionId":61387,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Is it easier to become popular nowadays?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61388","sourceQuestionId":61388,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Is it important for a teacher to be popular?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61389","sourceQuestionId":61389,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What are the qualities of being a good teacher?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61390","sourceQuestionId":61390,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Why are some students popular in school?"},{"id":"igopx-question-61391","sourceQuestionId":61391,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Why do people want to be popular?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61386","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["That's an interesting question.","While a teacher's popularity can be a positive sign, I don't believe it's a definitive indicator of their quality."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61387","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["I think it's a double-edged sword.","On one hand, social media provides a platform for anyone with a unique talent or idea to potentially reach a global audience overnight."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61388","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Of course.","While a degree of popularity can foster a positive learning environment, it is far less crucial than a teacher's core competency."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61389","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["I believe the most crucial qualities are expertise and empathy.","A great teacher not only masters the subject but also understands students' struggles, creating a supportive environment where everyone feels encouraged to ask questions and learn from mistakes."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61390","approach":"解释一至两个原因，用因果链说明行为如何产生，再承认人群差异。","example_direction":["Some students become popular because they're friendly and approachable.","They usually have good social skills, joining clubs or sports, which helps them connect with many people."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61391","approach":"解释一至两个原因，用因果链说明行为如何产生，再承认人群差异。","example_direction":["Well, I believe the primary drive is a fundamental human need for social acceptance and belonging.","Being popular often translates to having a wide social network, which can provide emotional support, reduce feelings of loneliness, and open doors to more opportunities, both personally and professionally."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-61386","text":"That's an interesting question. While a teacher's popularity can be a positive sign, I don't believe it's a definitive indicator of their quality. Truly great teachers are those who challenge their students and push them beyond their comfort zones, which isn't always a popular approach in the moment. The real mark of a good educator is the respect they earn from students for their expertise and dedication, even if their methods are demanding. Ultimately, their effectiveness is measured by the academic growth and long-term success of their students, not just their immediate likeability.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61387","text":"I think it's a double-edged sword. On one hand, social media provides a platform for anyone with a unique talent or idea to potentially reach a global audience overnight. On the other hand, this accessibility means the competition is fiercer than ever, and online fame can often be fleeting and superficial. So, while the path to popularity is more open, sustaining it is arguably much harder.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61388","text":"Of course. While a degree of popularity can foster a positive learning environment, it is far less crucial than a teacher's core competency. A truly effective educator commands respect through their expertise, passion for the subject, and genuine commitment to student growth, not merely through being liked. Ultimately, inspiring academic progress and critical thinking is a more significant, lasting legacy than transient popularity.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61389","text":"I believe the most crucial qualities are expertise and empathy. A great teacher not only masters the subject but also understands students' struggles, creating a supportive environment where everyone feels encouraged to ask questions and learn from mistakes. Ultimately, they inspire a genuine love for learning, which is far more valuable than just memorizing facts.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61390","text":"Some students become popular because they're friendly and approachable. They usually have good social skills, joining clubs or sports, which helps them connect with many people. A sense of humor also plays a big part.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-61391","text":"Well, I believe the primary drive is a fundamental human need for social acceptance and belonging. Being popular often translates to having a wide social network, which can provide emotional support, reduce feelings of loneliness, and open doors to more opportunities, both personally and professionally. For many, it’s also a sign of social validation, boosting their self-esteem and confidence.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%8F%97%E6%AC%A2%E8%BF%8E%E7%9A%84%E4%BA%BA&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8476&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-8666","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 节约时间的方法/改变","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8666,"passage":"<h2>节约时间的方法/改变</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-62637","sourceQuestionId":62637,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Do people who can manage time well become successful more easily?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62638","sourceQuestionId":62638,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Do you think parents should be responsible for teaching children to save time?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62639","sourceQuestionId":62639,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Does technology help people save time? How and why?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62640","sourceQuestionId":62640,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Is it necessary for children to learn time management?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62641","sourceQuestionId":62641,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What can people do to save time?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62642","sourceQuestionId":62642,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What can schools do to help students learn time management?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62637","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Yes, people with strong time management skills often find it easier to achieve success because they can focus on their goals and meet deadlines efficiently.","Good time management reduces stress and allows for better decision-making, which positively impacts productivity."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62638","approach":"明确主张，再解释理由和可能代价；必要时提出实施条件。","example_direction":["Yes, parents play an essential role in teaching children time management, as these skills are valuable throughout life.","By encouraging routines and prioritizing tasks, parents help children understand the importance of being organized."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62639","approach":"解释一至两个原因，用因果链说明行为如何产生，再承认人群差异。","example_direction":["Yes, technology greatly helps people save time by automating tasks and streamlining communication.","Apps and tools like email, messaging, and project management platforms make it easier to coordinate and complete work from anywhere."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62640","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Yes, learning time management is essential for children as it equips them with vital life skills.","By managing their time effectively, children can balance academic responsibilities, extracurricular activities, and personal time, which reduces stress and increases productivity."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62641","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["People can save time by planning their tasks in advance and setting clear priorities.","Using tools like calendars or to-do lists helps them stay organized and avoid unnecessary distractions."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62642","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Schools can play a pivotal role in teaching time management by incorporating structured lessons and practical strategies into the curriculum.","They could offer workshops that focus on prioritization, goal setting, and the effective use of planners or digital tools."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62637","text":"Yes, people with strong time management skills often find it easier to achieve success because they can focus on their goals and meet deadlines efficiently. Good time management reduces stress and allows for better decision-making, which positively impacts productivity. By using time wisely, they can balance work and personal life, maintaining both energy and motivation. Effective time management also builds a reputation for reliability, which is valuable in any career. Ultimately, it provides a clear path to accomplishing both short- and long-term goals.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62638","text":"Yes, parents play an essential role in teaching children time management, as these skills are valuable throughout life. By encouraging routines and prioritizing tasks, parents help children understand the importance of being organized. Simple habits, like setting time limits for activities and planning ahead, can be instilled from a young age. Teaching children to save time also promotes responsibility and reduces stress. This foundation helps them grow into efficient, focused adults.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62639","text":"Yes, technology greatly helps people save time by automating tasks and streamlining communication. Apps and tools like email, messaging, and project management platforms make it easier to coordinate and complete work from anywhere. Online shopping and banking services reduce the need for physical errands, saving people time on routine tasks. Smart devices, such as digital calendars and reminders, help people stay organized and avoid missed deadlines. Overall, technology simplifies many aspects of daily life, making tasks more convenient and efficient.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62640","text":"Yes, learning time management is essential for children as it equips them with vital life skills. By managing their time effectively, children can balance academic responsibilities, extracurricular activities, and personal time, which reduces stress and increases productivity. Early mastery of time management fosters discipline, enhances focus, and encourages independence. Moreover, it prepares children for the challenges of adulthood, helping them make informed decisions about how to allocate time for their priorities and goals.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62641","text":"People can save time by planning their tasks in advance and setting clear priorities. Using tools like calendars or to-do lists helps them stay organized and avoid unnecessary distractions. Delegating tasks when possible and focusing on one activity at a time are also effective ways to use time efficiently. Additionally, simple habits like preparing for the next day the night before can make mornings smoother. By being mindful of time, people can accomplish more with less stress.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62642","text":"Schools can play a pivotal role in teaching time management by incorporating structured lessons and practical strategies into the curriculum. They could offer workshops that focus on prioritization, goal setting, and the effective use of planners or digital tools. Teachers could also help students break down large tasks into manageable steps and provide guidance on balancing academic and extracurricular commitments. By fostering these skills, schools prepare students to manage their time efficiently, reducing stress and enhancing academic performance.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E8%8A%82%E7%BA%A6%E6%97%B6%E9%97%B4%E7%9A%84%E6%96%B9%E6%B3%95%2F%E6%94%B9%E5%8F%98&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8666&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-8692","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 送朋友的礼物","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":8692,"passage":"<h2>送朋友的礼物</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-62798","sourceQuestionId":62798,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Is it hard to choose a gift?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62799","sourceQuestionId":62799,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"When do people normally send gifts to others?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62800","sourceQuestionId":62800,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Which do people give on traditional festivals, red envelopes or other kinds of gifts?"},{"id":"igopx-question-62801","sourceQuestionId":62801,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Will people feel happy when receiving an expensive gift?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71228","sourceQuestionId":71228,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What do people usually consider when buying gifts?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71229","sourceQuestionId":71229,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Are there any unlucky things that people should not buy as gifts in your country?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62798","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Choosing a gift can be challenging, particularly when you want to find something meaningful and personal.","The difficulty often lies in selecting something that aligns with the recipient’s preferences, interests, and needs."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62799","approach":"先说明常见时机或场景，再解释原因，并考虑文化或人群差异。","example_direction":["People typically send gifts on special occasions such as birthdays, weddings, anniversaries, and holidays like Christmas or Lunar New Year.","Gifts are also given as gestures of appreciation, such as thanking someone for their help or support."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62800","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["On traditional festivals, especially in Chinese culture, giving red envelopes (hongbao) is a common practice, particularly during Lunar New Year.","These envelopes, usually filled with money, symbolize good luck, prosperity, and blessings for the recipient."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62801","approach":"区分预测与事实，说明变化驱动因素，并保留条件或不确定性。","example_direction":["While an expensive gift may initially excite the recipient due to its value or prestige, happiness from a gift is not solely determined by its price tag.","In many cases, the emotional connection or thoughtfulness behind the gift has a more lasting impact."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71228","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["When buying gifts, people usually consider the recipient's preferences, age, and the occasion.","Practicality is also important—nobody wants a useless gift."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71229","approach":"明确主张，再解释理由和可能代价；必要时提出实施条件。","example_direction":["Yes, there are several unlucky things to avoid as gifts in China.","A clock is the most famous taboo because 'giving a clock' sounds like 'attending a funeral'."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-62798","text":"Choosing a gift can be challenging, particularly when you want to find something meaningful and personal. The difficulty often lies in selecting something that aligns with the recipient’s preferences, interests, and needs. For example, choosing a gift for someone with very specific tastes or who already has everything can be tricky. Additionally, the occasion or the relationship between the giver and the receiver can also influence the choice. However, when you take the time to consider what would make the person happy or what might be useful, the process becomes more rewarding and thoughtful.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62799","text":"People typically send gifts on special occasions such as birthdays, weddings, anniversaries, and holidays like Christmas or Lunar New Year. Gifts are also given as gestures of appreciation, such as thanking someone for their help or support. In some cultures, gifts are exchanged to mark milestones or achievements, like graduations or promotions. Additionally, people may send gifts during times of celebration, or as a way to offer comfort, such as sending flowers or care packages during illness. Overall, gift-giving is a way to express feelings of love, gratitude, or goodwill.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62800","text":"On traditional festivals, especially in Chinese culture, giving red envelopes (hongbao) is a common practice, particularly during Lunar New Year. These envelopes, usually filled with money, symbolize good luck, prosperity, and blessings for the recipient. While red envelopes remain popular, people also exchange other types of gifts depending on the festival and personal preferences. For example, during Mid-Autumn Festival, mooncakes are often shared among family and friends. In recent years, some people opt for more modern gifts, like gift cards or digital red envelopes, blending tradition with convenience in the digital age.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-62801","text":"While an expensive gift may initially excite the recipient due to its value or prestige, happiness from a gift is not solely determined by its price tag. In many cases, the emotional connection or thoughtfulness behind the gift has a more lasting impact. For example, a carefully chosen, personalized gift can bring deeper joy, as it reflects the giver's understanding of the recipient's personality or needs. Ultimately, true happiness comes from the sentiment behind the gift and the relationship shared, rather than its monetary value. Expensive gifts can bring momentary pleasure but may not guarantee lasting happiness.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71228","text":"When buying gifts, people usually consider the recipient's preferences, age, and the occasion. Practicality is also important—nobody wants a useless gift. Budget is another key factor. In China, the meaning behind the gift matters a lot, like avoiding unlucky items. Beautiful packaging can also add value.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71229","text":"Yes, there are several unlucky things to avoid as gifts in China. A clock is the most famous taboo because 'giving a clock' sounds like 'attending a funeral'. Umbrellas are also avoided because they suggest separation. Pears are unlucky because the word sounds like 'leaving'. Sharp objects like knives symbolize cutting off relationships. Also, anything in sets of four is avoided because four sounds like death.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E9%80%81%E6%9C%8B%E5%8F%8B%E7%9A%84%E7%A4%BC%E7%89%A9&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=8692&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-9834","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 做困难的事情并成功的人","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9834,"passage":"<h2>做困难的事情并成功的人</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71172","sourceQuestionId":71172,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Is it difficult to do business in today's world?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71173","sourceQuestionId":71173,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"How can companies help protect the environment?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71174","sourceQuestionId":71174,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Does money equal success?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71175","sourceQuestionId":71175,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Other than making money, what is more important for a company?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71176","sourceQuestionId":71176,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Is it easy to start up a company?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71177","sourceQuestionId":71177,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"In which sectors are companies more likely to succeed in China?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71172","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Yes, it is quite challenging to do business in today's world.","Competition is fierce in almost every industry."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71173","approach":"说明具体方式、负责主体和作用机制，再举一种情境。","example_direction":["Companies can help protect the environment in several ways.","They can switch to renewable energy and improve energy efficiency in production."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71174","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["No, money does not equal success.","Money is only one measure of success."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71175","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["I think a company's reputation and social responsibility are more important than just making money.","A good company should care about its employees, customers, and the environment."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71176","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["It is relatively easy to register a company in China now, thanks to simplified procedures and low cost.","But making it survive and grow is very hard."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71177","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["In China, companies are more likely to succeed in technology and internet sectors, like AI, e-commerce, and short video platforms.","Consumer goods, especially food and beverage, also do well because of the huge domestic market."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71172","text":"Yes, it is quite challenging to do business in today's world. Competition is fierce in almost every industry. Costs like rent and labor are high, especially in big cities. Consumer preferences also change very quickly. However, the internet has lowered entry barriers for small startups, so those with a unique product or service can still succeed. It's difficult but not impossible.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71173","text":"Companies can help protect the environment in several ways. They can switch to renewable energy and improve energy efficiency in production. Designing recyclable products and reducing packaging waste is also crucial. Moreover, companies can promote paperless offices and remote work to cut carbon emissions. Corporate responsibility is essential for a greener future.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71174","text":"No, money does not equal success. Money is only one measure of success. True success also includes health, happiness, and meaningful relationships. A wealthy person with poor health and a broken family is not truly successful. On the other hand, a teacher who inspires students can be very successful without being rich. Money provides comfort, but it cannot buy love or fulfillment. So, success is multi-dimensional.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71175","text":"I think a company's reputation and social responsibility are more important than just making money. A good company should care about its employees, customers, and the environment. Long-term success depends on trust and innovation, not short-term profit. Ethical values and a positive culture are the real foundation.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71176","text":"It is relatively easy to register a company in China now, thanks to simplified procedures and low cost. But making it survive and grow is very hard. Competition is fierce, and many startups fail within two years. So starting up is easy; succeeding is difficult.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71177","text":"In China, companies are more likely to succeed in technology and internet sectors, like AI, e-commerce, and short video platforms. Consumer goods, especially food and beverage, also do well because of the huge domestic market. Green energy and healthcare are growing rapidly too, with strong government support.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%81%9A%E5%9B%B0%E9%9A%BE%E7%9A%84%E4%BA%8B%E6%83%85%E5%B9%B6%E6%88%90%E5%8A%9F%E7%9A%84%E4%BA%BA&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9834&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-9835","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 改变重要决定","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9835,"passage":"<h2>改变重要决定</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71179","sourceQuestionId":71179,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"When do most children begin to make their own decisions?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71179","approach":"先说明常见时机或场景，再解释原因，并考虑文化或人群差异。","example_direction":["Most children start making simple decisions around age three or four, like choosing what toy to play with or what snack to eat.","By primary school, they can decide how to spend their free time."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71179","text":"Most children start making simple decisions around age three or four, like choosing what toy to play with or what snack to eat. By primary school, they can decide how to spend their free time. In adolescence, they begin making bigger decisions about friendships and studies, though parents still guide them.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E6%94%B9%E5%8F%98%E9%87%8D%E8%A6%81%E5%86%B3%E5%AE%9A&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9835&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-9836","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 本地名人","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"2 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9836,"passage":"<h2>本地名人</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71181","sourceQuestionId":71181,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Is it always good to be a popular student at school?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71182","sourceQuestionId":71182,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Why are some students popular?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71181","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Being a popular student is not always good.","Popularity can bring social pressure and distractions from study."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71182","approach":"解释一至两个原因，用因果链说明行为如何产生，再承认人群差异。","example_direction":["Some students are popular because they have a good sense of humour and make others laugh.","Others are popular for their academic excellence or athletic skills."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71181","text":"Being a popular student is not always good. Popularity can bring social pressure and distractions from study. Some popular students become too concerned about maintaining their image. However, it can also build confidence and leadership skills. It depends on how the student handles it.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71182","text":"Some students are popular because they have a good sense of humour and make others laugh. Others are popular for their academic excellence or athletic skills. Kindness and willingness to help also make a student well-liked. Sometimes simply being confident and outspoken attracts people.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E6%9C%AC%E5%9C%B0%E5%90%8D%E4%BA%BA&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9836&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-9837","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 对结果开心的重要决定","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9837,"passage":"<h2>对结果开心的重要决定</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71184","sourceQuestionId":71184,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"How can we tell the difference between an important and an easy decision?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71185","sourceQuestionId":71185,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Do you think it is a good idea to make a small decision every day?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71186","sourceQuestionId":71186,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What little decisions do people make every day?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71187","sourceQuestionId":71187,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What if people in a group have different opinions on a decision?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71188","sourceQuestionId":71188,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Do you think most people's decisions are made in their 20s?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71189","sourceQuestionId":71189,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Which is better, to make a decision quickly or slowly?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71184","approach":"按同一标准比较两方，例如成本、便利或态度，并举对照例子。","example_direction":["An important decision usually has long-term consequences and is hard to reverse, like choosing a career or buying a house.","An easy decision is often reversible and has low stakes, like what to eat for lunch."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71185","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Yes, I think it's a good idea to make a small decision every day.","Small decisions train your decision-making muscle."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71186","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["People make numerous little decisions every day.","They decide what time to get up, what to eat for breakfast, and what clothes to wear."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71187","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["When a group disagrees, it's important to listen to all opinions first.","Then the group can discuss the pros and cons of each option."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71188","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["I think many important decisions are indeed made in one's twenties, but not all.","During this period, people choose their career path, often decide whether to pursue further education, and many meet their life partner."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71189","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["It depends on the nature of the decision.","For simple, reversible choices, making a quick decision is better—it saves time and energy."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71184","text":"An important decision usually has long-term consequences and is hard to reverse, like choosing a career or buying a house. An easy decision is often reversible and has low stakes, like what to eat for lunch. Important decisions require more time, information, and often affect other people.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71185","text":"Yes, I think it's a good idea to make a small decision every day. Small decisions train your decision-making muscle. They help build confidence and reduce hesitation. However, they should be low-risk and not take too much time. It's about progress, not perfection.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71186","text":"People make numerous little decisions every day. They decide what time to get up, what to eat for breakfast, and what clothes to wear. During work, they choose which task to tackle first. In the evening, they decide whether to exercise, watch TV, or go to bed early. Even scrolling the phone involves choosing what to click.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71187","text":"When a group disagrees, it's important to listen to all opinions first. Then the group can discuss the pros and cons of each option. If no consensus is reached, voting can be used. Sometimes it's wise to ask a neutral third party or an expert. The key is to respect differences and focus on the common goal.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71188","text":"I think many important decisions are indeed made in one's twenties, but not all. During this period, people choose their career path, often decide whether to pursue further education, and many meet their life partner. It's a time of transition and self-discovery. However, people continue to make important decisions later, like changing careers or moving cities. So the twenties are crucial, but not everything is decided then.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71189","text":"It depends on the nature of the decision. For simple, reversible choices, making a quick decision is better—it saves time and energy. But for complex, high-stakes decisions with long-term consequences, taking it slow and gathering enough information is wiser. A good decision-maker knows when to switch between fast and slow thinking.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%AF%B9%E7%BB%93%E6%9E%9C%E5%BC%80%E5%BF%83%E7%9A%84%E9%87%8D%E8%A6%81%E5%86%B3%E5%AE%9A&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9837&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-9838","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 快乐人士","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"3 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9838,"passage":"<h2>快乐人士</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71191","sourceQuestionId":71191,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Should teachers know what children are doing all the time?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71192","sourceQuestionId":71192,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Do you think teachers are able to spot unhappy children?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71193","sourceQuestionId":71193,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"How can arts spread positive emotions in society?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71191","approach":"明确主张，再解释理由和可能代价；必要时提出实施条件。","example_direction":["Teachers don't need to monitor children all the time.","Constant surveillance can make children feel anxious and suppressed."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71192","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Yes, I believe experienced teachers can often spot unhappy children.","They notice changes in behaviour, such as withdrawal or aggression."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71193","approach":"说明具体方式、负责主体和作用机制，再举一种情境。","example_direction":["Art has a unique power to spread positive emotions.","A beautiful song or a touching film can lift people's spirits instantly."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71191","text":"Teachers don't need to monitor children all the time. Constant surveillance can make children feel anxious and suppressed. But teachers should be aware of the general situation in the classroom, such as safety issues and signs of bullying. The key is to create a safe environment where children feel comfortable sharing, not to watch every move.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71192","text":"Yes, I believe experienced teachers can often spot unhappy children. They notice changes in behaviour, such as withdrawal or aggression. A sudden drop in academic performance is also a sign. However, some children hide their feelings very well, so teachers may not catch everyone. That's why regular emotional check-ins are important.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71193","text":"Art has a unique power to spread positive emotions. A beautiful song or a touching film can lift people's spirits instantly. Public art performances, like street concerts or community murals, create shared joy. Art therapy is also used to help people express emotions and heal. It touches the heart in a way words sometimes cannot.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%BF%AB%E4%B9%90%E4%BA%BA%E5%A3%AB&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9838&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-9839","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 看过的名人采访","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"7 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9839,"passage":"<h2>看过的名人采访</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71195","sourceQuestionId":71195,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What kinds of people are usually interviewed?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71196","sourceQuestionId":71196,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Why do some people dislike being interviewed?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71197","sourceQuestionId":71197,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Why do some people think interviews are waste of time?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71198","sourceQuestionId":71198,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What should people do to prepare for a job interview?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71199","sourceQuestionId":71199,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Why do we need to attend interviews when applying for jobs?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71200","sourceQuestionId":71200,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What should people wear to a job interview?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71201","sourceQuestionId":71201,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What kind of things do famous people often say in interviews?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71195","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Many types of people get interviewed.","Experts and professionals are interviewed for their knowledge on specific topics, like doctors or scientists."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71196","approach":"解释一至两个原因，用因果链说明行为如何产生，再承认人群差异。","example_direction":["Some people dislike being interviewed because they are shy or introverted.","Being in the spotlight makes them nervous."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71197","approach":"解释一至两个原因，用因果链说明行为如何产生，再承认人群差异。","example_direction":["Some people see interviews as a waste of time because many are repetitive and shallow.","They believe the interviewer just asks prepared questions without listening."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71198","approach":"明确主张，再解释理由和可能代价；必要时提出实施条件。","example_direction":["To prepare for a job interview, people should research the company and the role first.","They should prepare answers to common questions and think of examples to show their skills."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71199","approach":"解释一至两个原因，用因果链说明行为如何产生，再承认人群差异。","example_direction":["We need interviews because they help employers assess whether a candidate's skills and personality match the job.","A resume only shows past experience, but an interview reveals communication ability, attitude, and problem-solving skills."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71200","approach":"明确主张，再解释理由和可能代价；必要时提出实施条件。","example_direction":["People should wear professional and clean clothes to a job interview.","For most industries, business casual or a suit is safe."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71201","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Famous people often say things that are safe and positive.","They thank their fans and talk about hard work."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71195","text":"Many types of people get interviewed. Experts and professionals are interviewed for their knowledge on specific topics, like doctors or scientists. Celebrities are interviewed to promote their work. Ordinary people with unique experiences, like survivors or witnesses, are also interviewed for human-interest stories. Even job applicants are interviewed as part of the hiring process.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71196","text":"Some people dislike being interviewed because they are shy or introverted. Being in the spotlight makes them nervous. They may also fear saying the wrong thing and being misunderstood. For celebrities, repetitive questions can be boring. Some people value their privacy and don't want personal matters exposed.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71197","text":"Some people see interviews as a waste of time because many are repetitive and shallow. They believe the interviewer just asks prepared questions without listening. Also, some interviewers just want to create controversy for views. For job seekers, too many rounds of interviews without feedback feel inefficient.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71198","text":"To prepare for a job interview, people should research the company and the role first. They should prepare answers to common questions and think of examples to show their skills. Dressing appropriately and arriving early are also important. Practicing with a friend can boost confidence. Finally, prepare some questions to ask the interviewer.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71199","text":"We need interviews because they help employers assess whether a candidate's skills and personality match the job. A resume only shows past experience, but an interview reveals communication ability, attitude, and problem-solving skills. It also gives candidates a chance to learn about the company. It's a two-way evaluation.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71200","text":"People should wear professional and clean clothes to a job interview. For most industries, business casual or a suit is safe. The key is to look neat, conservative, and respectful. Avoid overly bright colors, strong perfume, and too much jewellery. Dressing appropriately shows you take the interview seriously.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71201","text":"Famous people often say things that are safe and positive. They thank their fans and talk about hard work. They usually avoid controversial topics. They also promote their new works or projects. Many give motivational quotes to inspire the audience.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E7%9C%8B%E8%BF%87%E7%9A%84%E5%90%8D%E4%BA%BA%E9%87%87%E8%AE%BF&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9839&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-9840","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 和朋友度过的愉快夜晚","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"1 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9840,"passage":"<h2>和朋友度过的愉快夜晚</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71203","sourceQuestionId":71203,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"How do people get along in a big family?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71203","approach":"说明具体方式、负责主体和作用机制，再举一种情境。","example_direction":["Getting along in a big family requires tolerance, communication, and respect for boundaries.","Members need to be understanding when sharing space and resources."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71203","text":"Getting along in a big family requires tolerance, communication, and respect for boundaries. Members need to be understanding when sharing space and resources. Everyone should do their part in household chores. Regular family meals help keep the bond strong. Avoiding gossip and being willing to compromise are also key.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%92%8C%E6%9C%8B%E5%8F%8B%E5%BA%A6%E8%BF%87%E7%9A%84%E6%84%89%E5%BF%AB%E5%A4%9C%E6%99%9A&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9840&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-9841","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 擅长做手工的人","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"6 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9841,"passage":"<h2>擅长做手工的人</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71205","sourceQuestionId":71205,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Do you think art classes are important for children?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71206","sourceQuestionId":71206,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Why do some children enjoy making things by hand?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71207","sourceQuestionId":71207,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Do children these days still like doing arts and crafts?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71208","sourceQuestionId":71208,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What impact can artistic buildings have on society?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71209","sourceQuestionId":71209,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Is it good to have creative people in a team?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71210","sourceQuestionId":71210,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"Does art, like music or theater, have an impact on society?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71205","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Yes, art classes are very important for children.","They encourage creativity and self-expression."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71206","approach":"解释一至两个原因，用因果链说明行为如何产生，再承认人群差异。","example_direction":["Children enjoy making things by hand because it is fun and gives them a sense of control.","They love the feeling of turning raw materials into something real."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71207","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Yes, many children still enjoy arts and crafts, although digital entertainment has taken up some time.","Schools still offer art classes, and DIY kits are very popular."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71208","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Artistic buildings can uplift a society.","They become landmarks and symbols of cultural identity."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71209","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Yes, having creative people in a team is highly valuable.","They bring new ideas and challenge old ways."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71210","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Yes, art has a profound impact on society.","Music and theater can unite people across differences."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71205","text":"Yes, art classes are very important for children. They encourage creativity and self-expression. Art helps develop fine motor skills and patience. It also offers a safe space for emotional release. Many children discover confidence and identity through creating something unique.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71206","text":"Children enjoy making things by hand because it is fun and gives them a sense of control. They love the feeling of turning raw materials into something real. It also gives them immediate feedback and a sense of achievement. Hands-on activities satisfy their natural curiosity and desire to explore.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71207","text":"Yes, many children still enjoy arts and crafts, although digital entertainment has taken up some time. Schools still offer art classes, and DIY kits are very popular. However, the motivation has shifted somewhat, from pure play to creating things to share on social media.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71208","text":"Artistic buildings can uplift a society. They become landmarks and symbols of cultural identity. They create public spaces that encourage social interaction. Good architecture also improves the visual environment and can even inspire economic regeneration. They make people feel proud of their city.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71209","text":"Yes, having creative people in a team is highly valuable. They bring new ideas and challenge old ways. Creative thinkers can solve problems that logic alone cannot. They inspire the whole team to think differently. A team without creativity becomes stagnant.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71210","text":"Yes, art has a profound impact on society. Music and theater can unite people across differences. They express emotions and ideas that words alone can't. Art also preserves culture and history. It can inspire social change and give voice to the voiceless. A society without art loses its soul.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E6%93%85%E9%95%BF%E5%81%9A%E6%89%8B%E5%B7%A5%E7%9A%84%E4%BA%BA&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9841&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true},{"id":"igopx-speaking-p3-9842","type":"speaking","title":"Part 3 · 听不感兴趣的话","book":"口语全集题目","part":3,"description":"3 个问题 · 练习笔记本机保存","relatedTopicId":9842,"passage":"<h2>听不感兴趣的话</h2><p>Part 3</p>","questions":[{"id":"igopx-question-71212","sourceQuestionId":71212,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What kind of topics do young people like to talk about today?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71213","sourceQuestionId":71213,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"What would happen if the listener didn't listen carefully?"},{"id":"igopx-question-71214","sourceQuestionId":71214,"type":"speaking","part":3,"text":"How can we tell if a listener is listening carefully?"}],"supportSections":[{"id":"answer_advice","title":"回答建议","origin":"ai_generated","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"topic_notes":["将个人故事提升为一般社会讨论，区分人群、场景或资源条件。","论证顺序可用观点、原因、具体例子、限制；避免绝对化判断。"],"question_advice":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71212","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["Young people today like to talk about entertainment, like new songs, films, and games.","They also discuss food and trendy places to visit."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71213","approach":"先表明判断，再解释原因并举例，最后补充一种例外或限制。","example_direction":["If the listener doesn't listen carefully, misunderstandings can happen.","The speaker may feel hurt and disrespected."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71214","approach":"说明具体方式、负责主体和作用机制，再举一种情境。","example_direction":["You can tell a listener is listening carefully if they maintain appropriate eye contact and nod at the right moments.","They will ask relevant follow-up questions."],"example_direction_origin":"website","practice":"先用自己的事实或观点回答，再用参考方向扩展，不逐字背诵。"}]}},{"id":"reference_answers","title":"网站参考回答","origin":"website","ui":{"collapsible":true,"default_collapsed":true},"content":{"items":[{"question_id":"igopx-question-71212","text":"Young people today like to talk about entertainment, like new songs, films, and games. They also discuss food and trendy places to visit. Topics about studies and careers are common as well. On social media, memes and funny videos are widely shared. Relationships and personal growth are also popular topics.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71213","text":"If the listener doesn't listen carefully, misunderstandings can happen. The speaker may feel hurt and disrespected. Important information might be missed, leading to mistakes later. In personal relationships, it can damage trust. So careless listening has real consequences.","origin":"website"},{"question_id":"igopx-question-71214","text":"You can tell a listener is listening carefully if they maintain appropriate eye contact and nod at the right moments. They will ask relevant follow-up questions. Their body language, like leaning forward, shows engagement. They also remember details and can summarize what you said.","origin":"website"}]}}],"source":{"url":"https://www.igopx.cn/examSpokenFollow?topicName=%E5%90%AC%E4%B8%8D%E6%84%9F%E5%85%B4%E8%B6%A3%E7%9A%84%E8%AF%9D&unitName=part2%263&materialName=%E5%8F%A3%E8%AF%AD%E5%85%A8%E9%9B%86%E9%A2%98%E7%9B%AE&topicId=9842&commitStatus=&smarterPracticeRecordId=","note":"题目来自用户提供的 igopx 题库，回答建议与网站参考回答分开展示"},"library":true}]);